window.STORIES = {"parts":[{"id":"p01","title":"Hello, Kyiv!","about":"First meetings: saying hello and sorry, talking about yourself and your friends, and making a plan together."},{"id":"p02","title":"Café and food","about":"Ordering in cafés and restaurants, shopping for food, cooking and baking at home, and going out for drinks."},{"id":"p03","title":"Shopping and money","about":"Shops, clothes, beauty and prices, paying and saving, buying online, and a first look at the fashion world."},{"id":"p04","title":"Getting around","about":"The metro, taxis, airports and hotels, scooters and cars, a road trip and planning a holiday."},{"id":"p05","title":"Phone and internet","about":"Your phone, laptop and the internet: signal and messages, email, buying online, fixing things and setting up a home office."},{"id":"p06","title":"Home and family","about":"Family and home life: relatives, a new flat, repairs and cleaning, a blackout, the dacha, pets, games, love and a wedding."},{"id":"p07","title":"Work and office","about":"Getting a job and working in an office: the interview, the first day, projects and meetings, feedback, and problems at work."},{"id":"p08","title":"School and study","about":"Classes and tests, languages and accents, maths homework, online courses, the library, school problems and research."},{"id":"p09","title":"Health and the doctor","about":"Being ill and getting better: the doctor and the dentist, checkups, healthy habits, stress, emergencies and talking openly about the body."},{"id":"p10","title":"Sport","about":"Watching and doing sport: football on TV, the gym, a marathon, martial arts, boxing, team games, the sea and extreme sports."},{"id":"p11","title":"Music, theater and art","about":"Bands and concerts, festivals and clubs, the opera and dancing, the theater and comedy, museums and street art."},{"id":"p12","title":"On screen","about":"Films, TV, radio and podcasts, video games and social media: what we watch, play and post."},{"id":"p13","title":"Nature and animals","about":"Animals at the zoo, in the park and on the farm, mountains and national parks, the sea, the climate and the history of life."},{"id":"p14","title":"Around the world","about":"Trips abroad with Anna, Max and their families: the words people use in other countries, from Paris to Kenya."},{"id":"p15","title":"Business and money","about":"How companies and money work: a small business, a startup, marketing, trade, banks and the stock market, the economy and big business."},{"id":"p16","title":"City, society and politics","about":"How a city and a country are run: city hall, volunteers, new neighbors, elections, parliament, protests, the news and the war."},{"id":"p17","title":"Law and crime","about":"Police, courts and crime: a stolen bike, a trial, gangs and drugs, a true-crime podcast and the fight against terror."},{"id":"p18","title":"Science and technology","about":"How computers, the internet, data, physics, chemistry, space, the brain and modern medicine work."},{"id":"p19","title":"History and religion","about":"Kings and empires, warriors and explorers, the dark times of the 20th century, and the world's faiths, myths and legends."},{"id":"p20","title":"Exclamations","about":"One-word reactions: little words of talk, surprise, feelings, laughter, shouts, sounds, gaming chat, hellos from other languages and words of faith."}],"chapters":[{"id":"c001","part":"p01","title":"Nice to meet you","level":"A1","words":["party","student","welcome","people","hello","nice","cool","good","friend","amigo","comrade"],"story":"It is Anna's first week at college in Kyiv. Tonight there is a [[party]] for new [[students|student]]. A man says, \"Hi, everyone, [[welcome]]!\" Many [[people]] smile and clap. Anna sees a tall boy alone. She says, \"[[Hello|hello]]! I am Anna.\" He says, \"I am Max. [[Nice|nice]] to meet you!\" They dance and laugh all night. The music is [[cool]], and the food is [[good]]. At the end, Anna and Max are [[friends|friend]]. Then Max's cousin Leo comes and says, \"Hey, [[amigo]]!\" Max and Leo were [[comrades|comrade]] at a sports camp. Now Kyiv feels like home to Anna."},{"id":"c002","part":"p01","title":"Lost on the first day","level":"A1","words":["trouble","ID","please","sorry","sir","moment","Miss","easy","OK","mister","Mrs.","madam","lady","gentleman"],"story":"Anna is late on her first day. At the door, she is in [[trouble]]. A guard says, \"Your [[ID]], [[please]].\" Anna opens her bag. \"[[Sorry|sorry]], [[sir]]. One [[moment]].\" Then she cannot find room twelve. A young woman sits at the desk. Anna asks, \"Excuse me, [[Miss]], where is it?\" \"It is [[easy]]. Go up and left.\" Anna says, \"[[OK]], thank you!\" On the stairs, an old man drops his keys. \"Excuse me, [[mister]], your keys!\" says Anna. In room twelve, the teacher is [[Mrs.]] Koval. Anna whispers, \"Good morning, [[madam]].\" The teacher smiles and says, \"Good morning, [[ladies|lady]] and [[gentlemen|gentleman]]!\" Anna sits down just in time."},{"id":"c003","part":"p01","title":"Tell Me About Yourself","level":"A1","words":["background","teenager","business","hobby","season","type","character","friendly","contact","goodbye"],"story":"After class, Anna and Max sit in the park. Anna asks Max about his [[background]]. He is from Odesa and is still a [[teenager]]. Anna's dad has a small [[business]], a flower shop. Max's [[hobby]] is taking pictures. Winter is Anna's favorite [[season]]. \"What [[type]] of music do you like?\" asks Max. \"Rock! I am a big fan,\" says Anna. She likes his [[character]], because he is so [[friendly]]. They swap phone numbers to stay in [[contact]]. Then Max says, \"[[Goodbye|goodbye]]! See you tomorrow!\""},{"id":"c004","part":"p01","title":"Anna's Photos","level":"A1","words":["photo","selfie","boyfriend","foot","face","blonde","hair","crazy","mood"],"story":"Anna shows Max her [[photos|photo]] on her phone. The first one is a [[selfie]] at the river. \"Who is this?\" asks Max. \"This is my [[boyfriend]], Oleh.\" He is six [[feet|foot]] tall, with a kind [[face]]. Next is a girl with long [[blonde]] [[hair]]. That is Anna's cousin Olya. The last picture shows Dima, her [[crazy]] friend. He is always in a good [[mood]]. Max laughs. \"Can I meet them all?\""},{"id":"c005","part":"p01","title":"A Plan for the Weekend","level":"A1","words":["idea","weekend","secret","chance","super","plan","sense","detail","fact"],"story":"Max has an [[idea]] for the [[weekend]]. \"Can you keep a [[secret]]?\" he asks Anna. \"My bro can give us his car. We have a [[chance]] to go to Lviv!\" Anna smiles. \"That is a [[super]] [[plan]]!\" It makes [[sense]], because the train is expensive. They talk about the [[details|detail]] over tea. Who drives? Where do they sleep? Now it is a [[fact]]: they leave on Saturday!"},{"id":"c006","part":"p02","title":"Lunch near college","level":"A1","words":["lunch","menu","soup","sandwich","dressing","rice","sauce","dessert","brunch"],"story":"Anna and Max have [[lunch]] near their college. They read the [[menu]]. Max orders [[soup]] and a [[sandwich]]. Anna wants a salad with [[dressing]]. She also takes chicken with [[rice]] and [[sauce]]. The food is hot and very tasty. For [[dessert]], Anna has cake and tea. Max eats half of her cake! Anna laughs. \"Next time, you pay!\" Max says, \"Deal! Sunday [[brunch]] is on me.\""},{"id":"c007","part":"p02","title":"Coffee before class","level":"A1","words":["coffee shop","vibe","hipster","barista","latte","blend","cappuccino","caramel","snob","croissant","espresso","cafe","bistro"],"story":"Max meets Anna at a [[coffee shop]] before class. The place has a great [[vibe]]. It is full of [[hipsters|hipster]] with laptops. The [[barista]] makes Anna a [[latte]]. It is from a new [[blend]]. Max orders a [[cappuccino]] with [[caramel]]. He tastes it slowly and nods. Anna laughs. \"You are a real coffee [[snob]]!\" They also take a [[croissant]]. Then Max wants a strong [[espresso]] too. They run to class, cups in hand. After class, they are very hungry. The [[cafe]] next door has only cakes. So they go to a little [[bistro]] for dinner."},{"id":"c008","part":"p02","title":"Pizza night","level":"A1","words":["chill","pizza","delivery","topping","pepperoni","mozzarella","salami","diameter","cola","nachos","snack","popcorn"],"story":"On Friday, Max wants to [[chill]] at home. Anna and two friends come over. They order a big [[pizza]] for [[delivery]]. \"What [[topping]] do we want?\" asks Anna. \"[[Pepperoni|pepperoni]] and [[mozzarella]]!\" says Max. His sister adds, \"And [[salami]] for me!\" It is huge, with a [[diameter]] of forty centimeters. They also get [[cola]], [[nachos]], and other [[snacks|snack]]. Then Max makes [[popcorn]], and they watch a movie. Soon everybody is asleep on the sofa."},{"id":"c009","part":"p02","title":"At the burger place","level":"A1","words":["fast food","junk food","drive-through","burger","hamburger","cheeseburger","ketchup","mayonnaise","milkshake","sundae","smoothie"],"story":"After the cinema, Max wants [[fast food]]. Anna laughs: \"That is [[junk food]], Max!\" Cars wait in line at the [[drive-through]]. But Anna, Max, and his cousin Ihor go inside. Every [[burger]] on the menu looks good. A [[hamburger]] has meat in a bun. A [[cheeseburger]] has meat and cheese. Max takes the cheese one with [[ketchup]] and [[mayonnaise]]. He also gets a chocolate [[milkshake]]. Anna takes a small [[sundae]]. Ihor wants fruit, so he orders a [[smoothie]]. Max has sauce on his nose, and they laugh."},{"id":"c010","part":"p02","title":"Sunday breakfast at home","level":"A2","words":["toaster","toast","jam","French toast","pancake","syrup","bacon","omelet","yogurt","grapefruit"],"story":"On Sunday morning, Anna's mama made a big breakfast. She put bread in the [[toaster]]. Soon there was hot [[toast]] with [[jam]] on the table. Then she dipped more bread in eggs and milk for [[French toast]]. Next came [[pancakes|pancake]] with sweet [[syrup]]. Dad cooked [[bacon]] and a cheese [[omelet]]. Anna ate everything and felt very happy. Only her brother Taras was on a diet. He ate just [[yogurt]] and half a [[grapefruit]]. But ten minutes later, his plate was full!"},{"id":"c011","part":"p02","title":"At the supermarket","level":"A1","words":["supermarket","broccoli","avocado","citrus","lemon","lime","tangerine","mandarin","mango","kiwi","cheddar","cracker"],"story":"Anna and Max go to the [[supermarket]]. Friends come for dinner tonight. Max puts [[broccoli]] and an [[avocado]] in the cart. Anna loves [[citrus]] fruit. She takes a yellow [[lemon]] and a green [[lime]]. Then she adds a [[tangerine]] and a [[mandarin]]. \"What is the difference?\" Max asks. Anna smiles, \"Both are small, orange, and sweet!\" They also take a big [[mango]] and four [[kiwis|kiwi]]. For snacks, they get [[cheddar]] and [[crackers|cracker]]. At the checkout, Max looks at the long bill. It is a big dinner!"},{"id":"c012","part":"p02","title":"Cooking for a Vegan Friend","level":"A2","words":["vegan","gluten","tofu","wok","kale","zucchini","curry","chili","hummus"],"story":"Anna invited her friend Lisa for dinner. Lisa is a [[vegan]], and she can't eat [[gluten]]. So Anna decided to cook [[tofu]] in a big [[wok]]. She added [[kale]] and [[zucchini]] too. Then she made a [[curry]] with one hot [[chili]]. She also made some [[hummus]] with fresh carrots. Lisa arrived, and they sat down to eat. Suddenly, Lisa smelled something strange. Anna forgot to turn off the gas! She ran to the kitchen and turned it off. Dinner was almost a fiasco, but the food was great."},{"id":"c013","part":"p02","title":"Baking a birthday cake","level":"A2","words":["ingredient","substitute","cinnamon","extract","blender","mixer","timer","cupcake","muffin","icing","cheesecake","brownie","tart","fudge","pecan","red velvet"],"story":"Anna and her mom bake for Grandma's birthday. First, they put all the [[ingredients|ingredient]] on the table. They have no sugar, so honey is their [[substitute]]. Mom adds [[cinnamon]] and a spoon of vanilla [[extract]]. Anna takes the [[blender]], but Mom says it is for drinks. So Anna turns on the [[mixer]], and Mom sets the [[timer]]. Soon twelve [[cupcakes|cupcake]] and six [[muffins|muffin]] come out of the oven. Anna puts pink [[icing]] only on the cupcakes. Then they make a [[cheesecake]] and a tray of [[brownies|brownie]]. Mom bakes an apple [[tart]], and Anna makes chocolate [[fudge]] with [[pecans|pecan]]. Last, they make Grandma's favorite [[red velvet]] cake. In the evening, Grandma tries everything and smiles."},{"id":"c014","part":"p02","title":"A barbecue at the dacha","level":"A2","words":["barbecue","propane","regulator","gas","hot dog","roast beef","grill","appetite","lemonade","marshmallow"],"story":"On Saturday Anna's family has a [[barbecue]] at the dacha. Dad connects the [[propane]] tank carefully. He checks the [[regulator]] twice. \"You can't be too careful with [[gas]],\" he says. Then he cooks [[hot dogs|hot dog]] for everyone. Later he puts a big piece of [[roast beef]] on the [[grill]]. After a day in the garden, everyone has a huge [[appetite]]. The kids drink cold [[lemonade]] in the shade. In the evening they roast [[marshmallows|marshmallow]] over the fire. Nobody wants to go back to the city."},{"id":"c015","part":"p02","title":"Dinner at an Italian restaurant","level":"A2","words":["hostess","spaghetti","ravioli","pasta","risotto","parmesan","truffle","mousse"],"story":"Max takes Anna to an Italian restaurant for her birthday. The [[hostess]] smiles and shows them to a table by the window. Max orders a glass of pinot, and Anna asks for water. Max chooses [[spaghetti]], and Anna wants [[ravioli]]. The chef makes all the [[pasta]] by hand. They also share a [[risotto]] with [[parmesan]] and black [[truffle]]. For dessert, they have chocolate [[mousse]]. Max drinks an espresso and pays the bill. \"Best birthday ever,\" says Anna."},{"id":"c016","part":"p02","title":"Mom's comfort food","level":"A2","words":["timing","comfort food","lasagna","mac and cheese","alfredo","lard","pudding","gelatin","lunch box"],"story":"After a hard week, Anna goes home to her parents. She arrives just as Mom takes dinner out of the oven. \"Perfect [[timing]]!\" says Mom. Tonight it's all Anna's favorite [[comfort food]]. They eat outside on the patio. There is hot [[lasagna]] and a bowl of [[mac and cheese]]. Dad loves the pasta [[alfredo]] most. Grandma's apple pie is made with [[lard]], like in the old days. For dessert there is chocolate [[pudding]] and cherry jelly with [[gelatin]]. Dad drinks a little brandy after dinner. Mom puts the rest of the food in Anna's [[lunch box]]."},{"id":"c017","part":"p02","title":"Street food Saturday","level":"A2","words":["food market","street food","kebab","taco","burrito","food truck","tortilla","guacamole","dip"],"story":"Anna and Max walk to a [[food market]] by the river. They want to try some [[street food]]. Max buys a big [[kebab]] first. Anna gets two [[tacos|taco]] and a [[burrito]] from a [[food truck]]. The cook makes warm [[tortillas|tortilla]] right in front of them. They also buy chips with [[guacamole]] and a spicy cheese [[dip]]. Max's face turns red, and he drinks a whole bottle of water. \"Too hot for you?\" Anna laughs."},{"id":"c018","part":"p02","title":"Happy hour","level":"A2","words":["happy hour","bar","bartender","barman","cocktail","martini","margarita","tequila","gin","tonic","lite","whiskey","bourbon","brandy","cognac","alcohol"],"story":"After a long week, Max's new colleagues invite him to [[happy hour]]. They meet at a small [[bar]], and Anna comes too. The young [[bartender]] is fast, and the old [[barman]] only pours beer. The young man makes [[cocktails|cocktail]] for everyone. Oleh orders a [[martini]], and Iryna gets a [[margarita]] with salt. Taras tries a shot of [[tequila]] with lime. Max asks for a [[gin]] and [[tonic]]. Their boss drinks a [[lite]] beer. At the next table, an old man orders [[whiskey]] and then [[bourbon]]. One of his friends has a [[brandy]], and the other has a [[cognac]]. Anna doesn't drink [[alcohol]], so she orders orange juice. By the end of the evening, Max knows everyone's name."},{"id":"c019","part":"p02","title":"Quiz night at the pub","level":"A2","words":["quiz","pub","ale","cider","lager","keg","darts","snooker"],"story":"Every Thursday there is a [[quiz]] at an Irish [[pub]] in town. Anna, Max and their friends make a team. The barman brings dark [[ale]] and sweet [[cider]]. Max orders a cold [[lager]] from a new [[keg]]. Anna drinks tea and answers all the history questions. Between rounds, they play [[darts]]. Max misses the board every time. Then he plays [[snooker]] and wins easily. At the end, their team gets second place and a free pizza."},{"id":"c020","part":"p03","title":"A new sweater","level":"A1","words":["shopping","shopping center","sweater","jumper","mannequin","cardigan","hoodie","sale","cotton","nylon","polyester","discount","coupon","voucher","cash","rebate"],"story":"Today Anna goes [[shopping]] at a big [[shopping center]]. She needs a warm [[sweater]] for winter. Her British friend Emma calls it a [[jumper]]. A [[mannequin]] in a window wears a red one. Next to it are a [[cardigan]] and a [[hoodie]]. Everything is on [[sale]]! Anna wants [[cotton]], not [[nylon]] or [[polyester]]. She gets a student [[discount]] and uses a [[coupon]]. Her mom's gift [[voucher]] pays for half. She pays the rest in [[cash]]. Later, the shop sends her a small [[rebate]]. Now her new blue sweater is almost free!"},{"id":"c021","part":"p03","title":"Max needs a new look","level":"A2","words":["style","fashion","boutique","outfit","brand","denim","baggy","tank top","beanie","tattoo","piercing"],"story":"Max wants a new [[style]], but he knows nothing about [[fashion]]. So Anna takes him to a small [[boutique]] in the city center. A shop assistant comes up to them. \"Can I help you, madam?\" she asks Anna. \"Yes, my friend needs a new [[outfit]],\" Anna says. First she chooses a gray hoodie from a good [[brand]]. Then she finds a [[denim]] jacket and [[baggy]] jeans. She also adds a white [[tank top]] and a green [[beanie]]. Max looks in the mirror and smiles. \"Maybe I need a [[tattoo]] now,\" he says. \"And a [[piercing]]?\" Anna laughs. \"One step at a time!\""},{"id":"c022","part":"p03","title":"At the beauty salon","level":"A2","words":["salon","stylist","styling","gel","manicure","cream","makeup","mascara","eyeliner","barber","afro"],"story":"Anna has a big party on Saturday. In the morning, she goes to a beauty [[salon]]. Her [[stylist]], Olena, is very kind. She does the [[styling]] with a little hair [[gel]]. Then Anna gets a [[manicure]]. After that, a nice hand [[cream]] makes her skin soft. At home, Anna does her [[makeup]] with [[mascara]] and [[eyeliner]]. Next door to the salon, Max goes to the [[barber]]. He sits next to a man with a big [[afro]]. At the party, Anna and Max both look great."},{"id":"c023","part":"p03","title":"A present for Mom","level":"A2","words":["pearl","bracelet","medallion","sapphire","opal","amethyst","expert","carat","crystal"],"story":"Anna and her brother Taras need a birthday present for Mom. They go to a small jewelry shop. First they look at white [[pearls|pearl]]. Then Taras finds a silver [[bracelet]] and a gold [[medallion]]. There are rings with a [[sapphire]], an [[opal]] and an [[amethyst]]. Everything is very expensive! An [[expert]] in the shop is very helpful. He explains what a [[carat]] is. Then he shows them a beautiful [[crystal]] on a thin chain. It is pretty and not expensive, so they buy it. Mom loves her present."},{"id":"c024","part":"p03","title":"Anna's student budget","level":"A1","words":["dollar","plus","minus","budget","cent","penny","dime","bank","balance","deposit","credit"],"story":"Today Anna counts her money. Her parents send her a hundred [[dollars|dollar]]. She has 50 more: 100 [[plus]] 50 is 150. Books cost 40, and 150 [[minus]] 40 is 110. Anna is on a tight [[budget]]. She saves every [[cent]] in a jar. A [[penny]] is one cent. A [[dime]] is ten cents. On Monday she goes to the [[bank]]. She checks her [[balance]] and makes a [[deposit]]. Anna wants a new phone, but not on [[credit]]. She saves for it instead."},{"id":"c025","part":"p03","title":"A parcel for Max","level":"A2","words":["online shopping","catalog","status","courier","product","defect","fake","marketplace"],"story":"Max loves [[online shopping]]. One evening he opens his favorite site. He finds great headphones in its [[catalog]]. He uses a coupon and saves ten dollars. Every day he checks the [[status]] of his order. On Friday a [[courier]] brings the box to his door. But the [[product]] does not look right. The left side is very quiet, so it has a [[defect]]. \"This is a [[fake]]!\" Max tells Anna. He sends it back and gets his money back. Then he buys real headphones from a good seller on a [[marketplace]]."},{"id":"c026","part":"p03","title":"Sofia's first fashion show","level":"B1","words":["fashion designer","fashion show","couture","supermodel","corset","cashmere","tweed","flannel","dandy","khaki","model","material","textile"],"story":"Max's sister Sofia is studying to be a [[fashion designer]]. On Saturday she shows her first collection at a small [[fashion show]] in Kyiv. It isn't real [[couture]], but every piece is made by hand. A tall [[supermodel]] opens the show in a black [[corset]] and a long red cape. Next come soft jackets in [[cashmere]], [[tweed]] and [[flannel]]. The last man, dressed like a [[dandy]], wears a smart suit in [[khaki]]. After the show, a shop owner asks about the tweed jacket. \"Every [[model]] in my collection comes in three colors,\" Sofia says proudly. Later, Anna asks her why she never uses nylon or polyester. \"Natural [[material]] like wool feels better on the skin,\" Sofia says. \"And good [[textiles|textile]] last for years.\" Her teacher says it is the best collection in the class."},{"id":"c027","part":"p04","title":"Around Kyiv by metro","level":"A1","words":["visitor","visit","transport","metro","inspector","escalator","center","downtown","avenue","park","monument","memorial","boulevard","promenade"],"story":"Anna's cousin Taras is her [[visitor]] today. It is his first [[visit]] to Kyiv. Anna loves public [[transport]], so they take the [[metro]]. An [[inspector]] checks their tickets. The long [[escalator]] takes them to the city [[center]]. They walk down a [[downtown]] [[avenue]] to the [[park]]. Taras takes photos of a big [[monument]]. Next to it is a quiet [[memorial]] with flowers. Then they walk along a green [[boulevard]]. The [[promenade]] by the river is their last stop. \"Excuse me, mister, your wallet!\" a woman calls. Taras says thank you and smiles."},{"id":"c028","part":"p04","title":"Taxi to the airport","level":"A1","words":["stuff","taxi","GPS","highway","terminal","shuttle"],"story":"Anna flies to London today. Max helps her with her [[stuff]]. They put two bags in a [[taxi]]. The driver turns on the [[GPS]]. He takes the [[highway]] to the airport. It is forty kilometers away. \"Thirty minutes max,\" he says. Soon they stop at the [[terminal]]. Free [[shuttle]] buses wait next to it. Anna hugs Max and runs inside."},{"id":"c029","part":"p04","title":"Anna's first flight","level":"A2","words":["chaos","baggage","passport","visa","control","duty-free","business class","steward","hub","transit","jet lag"],"story":"Anna's first flight starts with [[chaos]] at the airport. Her [[baggage]] weighs twenty kilograms, just right. She shows her [[passport]] and [[visa]] to the officer. Border [[control]] is quick and easy. At the [[duty-free]] she buys chocolate for her friends. Then she sees a celebrity going into [[business class]]! On the aeroplane, a friendly [[steward]] brings her coffee. She changes planes at a big [[hub]] in Europe. But her bag gets lost in [[transit]]. Her power converter is in that bag too! In London she has bad [[jet lag]] and no charger. The next day the bag arrives, and Anna laughs."},{"id":"c030","part":"p04","title":"Booking a hotel for the weekend","level":"A1","words":["hostel","motel","resort","hotel","booking","maximum","minimum","no-show","reception","check-in","max","Wi-Fi","adapter","converter","check-out"],"story":"Max looks for a cheap weekend in Lviv. A [[hostel]] is cheap, but the rooms are shared. A [[motel]] is for drivers on the road. A [[resort]] costs too much. So Max finds a small [[hotel]]. His [[booking]] is for four people [[maximum]]. The [[minimum]] stay is two nights. A [[no-show]] costs a fee. On Friday at [[reception]], [[check-in]] takes two minutes [[max]]. They get the [[Wi-Fi]] password and a phone [[adapter]]. Max's old speaker needs a [[converter]] too. [[Check-out|check-out]] is at eleven on Sunday."},{"id":"c031","part":"p04","title":"A night in a luxury hotel","level":"A2","words":["luxury","concierge","foyer","hall","corridor","deluxe","king-size","queen-size","jacuzzi","spa","massage","sauna","premium","high-end","room service"],"story":"Anna wins a night in a [[luxury]] hotel in a radio competition. A smiling [[concierge]] meets her in the [[foyer]]. They walk through a big [[hall]] and down a long [[corridor]]. \"This is a [[deluxe]] room,\" he says. The bed is [[king-size]], even bigger than a [[queen-size]] bed. There is a [[jacuzzi]] in the bathroom too. In the evening she tries the [[spa]]. First she gets a back [[massage]], then she relaxes in the [[sauna]]. Everything is [[premium]], and even the coffee machine is [[high-end]]. In the morning she orders breakfast from [[room service]]. She sends Max a photo: \"I never want to go home!\""},{"id":"c032","part":"p04","title":"Max's new scooter","level":"A2","words":["moped","scooter","asphalt","biker","limit","tunnel","bicycle","reflector","pedal","incident","biking","mountain bike"],"story":"Max wants to get to college faster. A [[moped]] is too noisy, so he buys an electric [[scooter]]. On Monday he rides on the smooth [[asphalt]] by the river. A [[biker]] on a loud motorcycle passes him. Max goes faster and forgets the speed [[limit]]. In a dark [[tunnel]] he almost hits a [[bicycle]]. Luckily, he sees its red [[reflector]] just in time. The cyclist stops, her foot still on the [[pedal]]. \"Slow down!\" she shouts. After this [[incident]], Max rides slowly. On weekends he goes [[biking]] in the forest on his [[mountain bike]]."},{"id":"c033","part":"p04","title":"Dad buys a car","level":"A2","words":["enthusiast","grand prix","automobile","auto","showroom","supercar","limousine","sedan","diesel","minivan","motor","test drive","leasing"],"story":"Anna's dad is a car [[enthusiast]]. He watches every [[grand prix]] on TV. Now he wants a new [[automobile]] for the family. On Saturday they go to an [[auto]] dealer with a big [[showroom]]. Dad stops next to a red [[supercar]]. Then he looks at a long white [[limousine]]. \"Too expensive, Dad,\" Anna laughs. So he chooses between a [[sedan]] and a [[diesel]] [[minivan]]. Anna's driving instructor comes too and listens to the [[motor]]. Dad takes the minivan for a [[test drive]]. Then he asks the manager about [[leasing]]. Next week the family drives home in a new car."},{"id":"c034","part":"p04","title":"The car breaks down","level":"A2","words":["accelerator","mechanic","garage","compressor","carburetor","chassis","bumper"],"story":"On the way to the dacha, Dad presses the [[accelerator]]. But the car slows down, and the motor stops. Anna calls a [[mechanic]] from a small auto repair shop. He comes quickly and takes the car to his [[garage]]. There he uses a very loud air [[compressor]]. He cleans the [[carburetor]], and the car starts again. He also checks the [[chassis]], and it is fine. Then he finds a crack in the [[bumper]] and fixes it. Dad pays, and the family gets to the dacha for dinner."},{"id":"c035","part":"p04","title":"A road trip in America","level":"A2","words":["road trip","camper","jeep","turbo","off-road","holder","pickup"],"story":"Max and his cousin Ivan go on a [[road trip]] in America. Uncle Petro drives a [[camper]], and the boys have an old [[jeep]]. It has a [[turbo]], so it is fast. They take an [[off-road]] path into the hills. Max's phone sits in a [[holder]] and shows the map. At a gas station, gas costs four dollars a gallon. In the evening they follow a [[pickup]] to a cheap motel. Each boy eats a huge cheeseburger. Uncle Petro tries a bourbon and makes a funny face. Everyone sleeps well after a long day."},{"id":"c036","part":"p04","title":"Planning a summer trip","level":"A1","words":["trip","bureau","agent","tour operator","low-cost","nonstop","charter","tour","guide","tourism","tourist","travel agent"],"story":"Anna and Max want a [[trip]] in August. They go to a travel [[bureau]] in Kyiv. An [[agent]] meets them with a smile. She works for a big [[tour operator]]. She shows them a [[low-cost]] flight. This plane flies [[nonstop]] to the coast. A [[charter]] is cheap too. Or they take a bus [[tour]] with a [[guide]]. \"[[Tourism|tourism]] is very big this year,\" she says. \"Every [[tourist]] wants to go to the sea.\" Max says, \"You are a great [[travel agent]]!\" They book two bus seats and smile."},{"id":"c037","part":"p04","title":"Uncle Ivan, the pilot","level":"A2","words":["pilot","cockpit","jet","radar","transponder","sonar","autopilot","helicopter","rotor","propeller","aeroplane","glider","ace","parachute","simulator"],"story":"Max's Uncle Ivan is a [[pilot]]. One Saturday he took Max and Anna to the airport. They sat in the [[cockpit]] of his big [[jet]]. \"This is the [[radar]], and this is the [[transponder]],\" he said. \"Ships use [[sonar]] under the water, but we use radar.\" Anna asked, \"Does the [[autopilot]] fly the plane for you?\" At a small airfield, a [[helicopter]] landed with a very loud [[rotor]]. Next to it stood an old plane with a [[propeller]]. \"My grandpa called it an [[aeroplane]],\" Uncle Ivan said with a smile. \"My old teacher flies that [[glider]], and he is a real [[ace]].\" Then a man jumped from a plane with a red [[parachute]]. That evening Max practiced on a flight [[simulator]] for hours."},{"id":"c038","part":"p05","title":"Anna's new smartphone","level":"A2","words":["smartphone","camera","zoom","touchscreen","sensor","Bluetooth","ringtone","device","gadget","telephone"],"story":"Anna's old phone broke, so she went shopping with Max. She wanted a high-end [[smartphone]] this time. \"This one has a very fast chip,\" the shop assistant said. He showed her the [[camera]] and its strong [[zoom]]. Anna touched the big [[touchscreen]], and the display was bright and clear. Her finger on the [[sensor]] opened the phone at once. The assistant connected her headphones by [[Bluetooth]]. He also changed her [[ringtone]] to a happy song. \"It's an expensive [[device]],\" Anna said quietly. \"But it's the best [[gadget]] in the shop,\" Max said. That evening, Anna called Grandma on her old home [[telephone]]. Grandma laughed, \"You sound so clear today!\""},{"id":"c039","part":"p05","title":"No signal in the metro","level":"A1","words":["signal","internet","online","offline","message","SMS","chat","roaming"],"story":"Anna is in the metro. Her phone has no [[signal]]. There is no [[internet]] here. She cannot go [[online]]. Anna is [[offline]] for an hour. Then she walks up to the street. Her phone gets twenty [[messages|message]]. There is also an [[SMS]] from Mama. Max writes in the group [[chat]]: \"Where are you?\" Then Mama calls: \"Why is your [[roaming]] on?\" Anna laughs and turns it off."},{"id":"c040","part":"p05","title":"Max fixes Anna's laptop","level":"A2","words":["laptop","glitch","IT","computer","software","hardware","backup","file","USB","cable","update","reset","upgrade","shortcut","desktop"],"story":"Anna's [[laptop]] was slow and full of [[glitches|glitch]]. So she called Max, who works in [[IT]]. He connected it to his own [[computer]] at home. Soon he found the problem in the [[software]], not the [[hardware]]. \"First, let's make a [[backup]] of every [[file]],\" he said. He saved them on a disk with a [[USB]] [[cable]]. Then he installed an [[update]] and did a [[reset]]. \"Next year, you need a memory [[upgrade]],\" Max said. He also showed her a keyboard [[shortcut]] for copying text. \"It works like new now!\" Anna said happily. \"My [[desktop]] at work is still faster,\" Max joked."},{"id":"c041","part":"p05","title":"An email to the professor","level":"A2","words":["email","user","account","username","template","header","slash","format","inbox","reply","spam","link"],"story":"Anna had to write her first [[email]] in English to a professor. She was a new [[user]] of the university mail app. She logged in to her [[account]] with her [[username]]. Then she chose a simple [[template]]. She put her name in the [[header]]. She put a [[slash]] between the day and the month. Then she attached her homework in PDF [[format]]. All evening she checked her [[inbox]], but nothing came. Max said, \"Maybe his [[reply]] is in [[spam]].\" He was right! The professor thanked her and sent a [[link]] to a reading list."},{"id":"c042","part":"p05","title":"Train tickets online","level":"A2","words":["online service","web","website","browser","site","web browser","layout","browsing","pop-up","click","code","screenshot","QR code","scan"],"story":"Anna wanted train tickets to Lviv, so she tried an [[online service]]. Max found it on the [[web]] for her. The [[website]] opened very slowly in her phone [[browser]]. So she opened the [[site]] in the [[web browser]] on her laptop. The [[layout]] was confusing, and she could not find the tickets. While [[browsing]], she closed three [[pop-ups|pop-up]]. Finally, with one [[click]], she bought tickets for her and Max. Then she entered the [[code]] from a text message. She took a [[screenshot]] of the [[QR code]] for the trip. On the train, the conductor checked her phone. Anna showed him a [[scan]] of her student card too. Everything was fine, and the trip began."},{"id":"c043","part":"p05","title":"Max's new flat goes online","level":"A2","words":["provider","router","modem","connector","antenna","home office","setup","headset","monitor","display","microphone","printer","cartridge","scanner"],"story":"Max's new flat had no internet. On Monday, a technician from his [[provider]] came. He brought a [[router]] and a [[modem]]. He fixed a bad [[connector]] and moved the [[antenna]] on the roof. Then Max made a small [[home office]] in his bedroom. His new [[setup]] had a [[headset]] and a big [[monitor]]. Its [[display]] was bright and clear. He also got a good [[microphone]] for video calls. He bought an old [[printer]], but it needed a new [[cartridge]]. Anna brought him her old [[scanner]] as a housewarming gift. \"Now I can work from home!\" Max said happily."},{"id":"c044","part":"p06","title":"Anna's family tree","level":"A1","words":["sibling","sis","bro","trimester","placenta","baby","cousin","clan","pensioner","mama","optimist","realist"],"story":"Anna draws her family tree for Max. Her parents and two [[siblings|sibling]] are on it. Her brother Taras calls her \"[[sis]].\" She calls him \"[[bro]].\" Aunt Olha is in her last [[trimester]]. The [[placenta]] and the [[baby]] are healthy. Soon Anna has a new [[cousin]]! \"Your [[clan]] is very big!\" Max says. Grandpa is an old admiral, now a [[pensioner]]. [[Mama|mama]] laughs and says, \"Grandpa is a true [[optimist]].\" \"And Grandma is a [[realist]],\" Anna adds. \"You are just like Grandpa,\" Max smiles."},{"id":"c045","part":"p06","title":"A surprise party for Mama","level":"A2","words":["surprise","invite","bouquet","florist","confetti","photo album","scrapbook","liqueur","karaoke","compliment"],"story":"Anna and her brother Taras planned a [[surprise]] party for Mama's birthday. They sent an [[invite]] to the whole family. Taras ordered a big [[bouquet]] from a [[florist]] near their home. When Mama came home, everyone shouted and threw [[confetti]]. Anna found old family pictures in a dusty [[photo album]]. She glued the best ones into a colorful [[scrapbook]] for Mama. Mama cried happy tears. Her friend Lida brought a cake with coffee [[liqueur]]. Then they all sang [[karaoke]] until late. Mama paid her kids a sweet [[compliment]]: \"You are the best!\""},{"id":"c046","part":"p06","title":"Max's new loft","level":"A2","words":["realtor","penthouse","townhouse","condominium","loft","interior","sofa","decor","mini","intercom","thermostat","comfort"],"story":"Max wanted to move out of his parents' home. A [[realtor]] showed him a [[penthouse]] on the top floor. It had a great view, but the price was crazy. Then she showed him a [[townhouse]] with its own small garden. It was nice, but a whole house was too big. Next came an apartment in a [[condominium]], but the fees were high. At last, she showed him a small [[loft]] in an old building. The [[interior]] was modern, and an old [[sofa]] stood by the window. The [[decor]] was simple, and there was a [[mini]] fridge. Max tested the [[intercom]] and the [[thermostat]]. The room was small, but Max loved its [[comfort]]. \"I'll take it!\" he said with a big smile."},{"id":"c047","part":"p06","title":"Fixing Things at Home","level":"A2","words":["professional","drill","metal","bolt","mechanism","panel","block","cement","primer","adhesive","siding","vibrator"],"story":"Anna's dad and Taras did not want to call a [[professional]]. \"We can fix the flat ourselves,\" Dad said. First, Taras used a [[drill]] to make holes for [[metal]] shelves. They used [[bolts|bolt]] five millimeters wide. Then Dad repaired the [[mechanism]] in the door lock. He also checked the electrical [[panel]]. They built a small wall with concrete [[blocks|block]] and [[cement]]. Next, they painted it with [[primer]]. Their neighbor used a strong [[adhesive]] for his [[siding]]. He also had a loud concrete [[vibrator]] for his new steps. Dad laughed, \"Next time, we'll ask him for help!\""},{"id":"c048","part":"p06","title":"A Winter Blackout","level":"A2","words":["blackout","generator","beep","kerosene","quilt","boiler","radiator","detector","hypothermia"],"story":"One cold January evening, there was a [[blackout]] in Anna's building. Dad turned on the [[generator]] in the yard. It gave a loud [[beep]] and started working. Mama lit an old [[kerosene]] lamp. Anna wrapped herself in Grandma's warm [[quilt]]. Slowly the [[boiler]] and the [[radiator]] got cold. Suddenly the smoke [[detector]] went off because of the lamp! Taras opened the window for a minute. \"Don't worry, nobody will get [[hypothermia]] tonight,\" Mama joked. At midnight the lights came back on."},{"id":"c049","part":"p06","title":"Cleaning day","level":"A2","words":["cleaner","plastic","recycling","compost","container","cycle","detergent","dispenser","filter","spray","aerosol","alarm","alert"],"story":"On Saturday, Max's apartment is a big mess. He calls a [[cleaner]], and Oksana arrives at ten. She puts all the [[plastic]] in the [[recycling]] bin. Old food goes into the [[compost]] on the balcony. She puts the leftovers in a [[container]] in the fridge. Max chooses a short [[cycle]] but adds too much [[detergent]]. Soon there are bubbles all over the bathroom floor! Oksana laughs and fills the soap [[dispenser]] with the extra soap. She changes the coffee [[filter]] and cleans the windows with a [[spray]]. Then she uses an [[aerosol]] near the kitchen fire [[alarm]]. It beeps loudly, and an [[alert]] pops up on Max's phone. They both laugh, and soon the apartment is clean and fresh."},{"id":"c050","part":"p06","title":"A weekend at the dacha","level":"A2","words":["cottage","bungalow","villa","chalet","veranda","hammock","gnome","patio","garden center","dahlia","iris","azalea","jasmine","magnolia","sprinkler"],"story":"Anna and Max visit Grandma's [[cottage]] at the dacha. Her neighbor has a small [[bungalow]], and another has a big [[villa]]. \"I don't need a [[chalet]] or a palace,\" Grandma smiles. They drink tea on the [[veranda]], and Max sleeps in the [[hammock]]. A funny garden [[gnome]] stands next to the stone [[patio]]. In the morning, Grandma goes to the [[garden center]] for seeds. She comes back with seeds for her red [[dahlias|dahlia]]. Anna helps her plant a purple [[iris]] and a pink [[azalea]]. In the evening, the [[jasmine]] and the [[magnolia]] smell sweet. Then Anna turns on the [[sprinkler]] and gets Max all wet! He laughs and says, \"Now I am a flower too!\""},{"id":"c051","part":"p06","title":"Taras wants a pet","level":"A2","words":["pet shop","aquarium","koi","carp","iguana","microchip","temperament"],"story":"Anna's little brother Taras really wants a pet. On Sunday, Anna takes him to the [[pet shop]]. First they look at a big [[aquarium]] with orange [[koi]]. \"Are they goldfish?\" Taras asks. \"No, they are a kind of [[carp]],\" the seller explains. Taras loves the green [[iguana]], but Anna says it is too big. Then they see three little dogs. The white puppy is calm and quiet. The seller says, \"This one already has a [[microchip]].\" She also says it has a gentle [[temperament]] and loves children. Taras smiles and asks, \"Can we come back with Mom?\""},{"id":"c052","part":"p06","title":"Games night at Grandma's","level":"A2","words":["puzzle","crossword","bingo","mahjong","gambit","endgame","tarot","horoscope","zodiac"],"story":"On Friday, the family has a games night at Grandma's. Anna and Max start a big [[puzzle]] on the table. Grandpa does a [[crossword]] and asks everyone for help. Then they play [[bingo]], and Mom wins a chocolate bar. Grandma teaches Max how to play [[mahjong]]. Later Grandpa plays chess with Max and starts with a clever [[gambit]]. Max fights hard, but Grandpa wins the [[endgame]]. At the end, Grandma reads [[tarot]] cards for everyone. She also reads everyone's [[horoscope]] from the newspaper. Then she asks Max about his [[zodiac]] sign and smiles. \"Max will win next Friday!\" she says."},{"id":"c053","part":"p06","title":"Anna Babysits","level":"A2","words":["babysitter","activity","pirate","monster","zombie","sticker","glitter","carousel","clown","pony","buffoon","collage","boy scout"],"story":"On Saturday, Anna is the [[babysitter]] for the neighbors' kids. Lev is eight, and Mila is five. Anna has a list of fun [[activities|activity]] for the day. First Lev dresses up as a [[pirate]], and Mila is an angel. They play a game about a scary [[monster]] and a slow [[zombie]]. Mila gets scared, so they make cards with [[stickers|sticker]] and [[glitter]]. After lunch, they go to the park and ride the [[carousel]]. Nearby, a [[clown]] gives free rides on a [[pony]]. Lev runs around and acts like a silly [[buffoon]], and Mila laughs. At home, they make a [[collage]] about their day. Then Lev's big brother comes home in his [[boy scout]] uniform. The kids ask him, \"Can Anna come again next Saturday?\""},{"id":"c054","part":"p06","title":"Max on a dating app","level":"A2","words":["dating","profile","sexy","sex","ex","narcissist","red flag","crush","rendezvous","fetish","love story"],"story":"Max is single, so he tries a [[dating]] app. Anna helps him with his [[profile]] and his photo. Max asks, \"Do I look [[sexy]] here?\" Anna laughs and says, \"Write about your hobbies, not about [[sex]].\" Then Max sees his [[ex]], a real [[narcissist]], on the app. \"She never listened to you. That was a [[red flag]],\" Anna says. Suddenly Max gets a message from Lina, his [[crush]] from the gym! She studies history and invites him to a [[rendezvous]] at the museum. She shows him a [[fetish]], a holy wooden object from long ago. Max smiles: maybe this is the start of a [[love story]]."},{"id":"c055","part":"p06","title":"Sofia's Coming Out","level":"B1","words":["coming out","queer","partner","gender","LGBT","gay","taboo","respect"],"story":"On Sunday, Max's sister Sofia invites the whole family for dinner. She is nervous, because this dinner is her [[coming out]]. \"I am [[queer]],\" she says, \"and I want you to meet my [[partner]], Dana.\" For a moment the room is quiet, and then Max gives his sister a big hug. Grandma asks many questions, and Dana kindly explains [[gender]] and what [[LGBT]] means. \"Is queer the same as [[gay]]?\" Grandma asks, and Dana says some people use both words. Dad admits that he believed an old stereotype from TV. Mom says that in her family, talking about feelings was always a [[taboo]]. \"Not in this family,\" Grandma says, and she pours tea for Dana first. Max raises his glass: \"To Sofia and Dana, with love and [[respect]]!\""},{"id":"c056","part":"p06","title":"Cousin Olya's wedding","level":"A2","words":["coordinator","catering","tiara","video camera","kilt","speech","DJ","millennium","forever"],"story":"Anna's cousin Olya gets married on Saturday. An event [[coordinator]] plans everything for the big day. The banquet is in a beautiful old hotel. The [[catering]] is excellent, and the cake is huge. Olya wears a white dress and a small silver [[tiara]]. Max films everything with his dad's old [[video camera]]. The groom's friend Ian is from Scotland, and he wears a [[kilt]]. Ian makes a funny [[speech]]. Then he acts like a buffoon with a flower on his head! Later the [[DJ]] plays a slow waltz for the happy couple. Grandma says, \"This is the best party since the new [[millennium]]!\" Olya smiles: \"I will remember this day [[forever]].\""},{"id":"c057","part":"p07","title":"Max's job interview","level":"A2","words":["part-time","recruiter","blazer","interviewer","skill","soft skill","portfolio","aspect","offer","contract"],"story":"Max is a student, but he wants a [[part-time]] job. He dreams of becoming a software engineer. On Monday, a [[recruiter]] from an IT company calls him. On Wednesday, Max wears his new [[blazer]] to the interview. The [[interviewer]] is a friendly woman named Iryna. She asks about his [[skills|skill]] in coding. Then she asks about teamwork, an important [[soft skill]]. Max shows his [[portfolio]] with three small apps. He asks about every [[aspect]] of the job, like hours and pay. Two days later, Max gets an [[offer]]! On Friday, he reads the [[contract]] carefully and signs it."},{"id":"c058","part":"p07","title":"Max's First Office Day","level":"A1","words":["office","HR","badge","office manager","assistant","dress code","training","meeting room","administrator","admin"],"story":"It is Friday, Max's first day at the [[office]]. A woman from [[HR]] gives him a [[badge]]. He meets his boss and the [[office manager]]. Kate, the [[assistant]], tells him about the [[dress code]]. Max looks down at his old jeans. Kate laughs: \"Jeans are OK on Fridays!\" At ten, the [[training]] starts in the [[meeting room]]. But Max's computer does not work. Kate calls the system [[administrator]], Oleh. \"Everybody here calls me the [[admin]],\" Oleh says. He fixes the computer fast. Max thinks, \"I like this new job.\""},{"id":"c059","part":"p07","title":"A new project","level":"A2","words":["period","leader","project","client","task","deadline","milestone","wiki","checklist","enthusiasm","overkill"],"story":"It is a busy [[period]] at Max's work. The team [[leader]], Olena, starts a new [[project]] for a big [[client]]. The manager, Pavlo, gives Max his first [[task]] with a Friday [[deadline]]. Pavlo writes every [[milestone]] on the team [[wiki]]. Max also makes his own [[checklist]] with ten small steps. He works with great [[enthusiasm]]. He even sets three alarms for one meeting. Pavlo laughs: \"Three alarms? That is [[overkill]]!\" On Thursday, Max finishes everything early, and the client is happy."},{"id":"c060","part":"p07","title":"Max's first presentation","level":"A2","words":["projector","slide","document","service","feedback","follow-up","insight","impact","deep dive"],"story":"On Monday, Max gives his first presentation to the client. He is nervous, and the [[projector]] does not turn on at first. Finally, his first [[slide]] appears on the wall. Max talks about a [[document]] on the client's new delivery [[service]]. The client listens carefully and asks many questions. The next day, she sends her [[feedback]] in a long email. Then her team sends a [[follow-up]] with some useful [[insights|insight]]. They like the [[impact]] of the work on their sales. They ask for a [[deep dive]] into the numbers next week. Max smiles: his first presentation was a success."},{"id":"c061","part":"p07","title":"A One-on-One with the Boss","level":"A2","words":["one-on-one","supervisor","performance review","progress","potential","professionalism","director","bonus","boost","boss","manager","one-to-one"],"story":"Max has worked at the office for three months. Today he has a [[one-on-one]] meeting with Ms. Lee, his [[supervisor]]. It is his first [[performance review]], and he feels nervous. Ms. Lee smiles and talks about his [[progress]] on the new project. \"You have real [[potential]],\" she says. She also likes his [[professionalism]] with difficult clients. Then the [[director]] comes in with an envelope. Inside is a small [[bonus]] for Max! The good news gives him a big [[boost]]. That evening, Max tells Anna, \"My [[boss]] is great!\" \"Which one, the supervisor or the [[manager]]?\" Anna asks. Max laughs and says, \"Both! And next month I get [[one-to-one]] English lessons.\" Then he buys pizza for Anna and their friends."},{"id":"c062","part":"p07","title":"Sofia Works Freelance","level":"A2","words":["freelancer","freelance","invoice","calendar","task manager","time management","coaching","networking","work-life balance"],"story":"On Saturday, Max visits his sister Sofia and says, \"Hey, sis!\" Sofia is a [[freelancer]], and she works from home. She started [[freelance]] work after she left her old office. Right now she is writing an [[invoice]] for a client. On the wall there is a big [[calendar]] with colorful notes. She plans her week in a [[task manager]] app too. \"I read a lot about [[time management]],\" she says. Last month she tried career [[coaching]] online. Her coach told her that [[networking]] brings new clients. \"But do you ever rest?\" Max asks. Sofia laughs and closes her laptop. \"For me, [[work-life balance]] is important!\""},{"id":"c063","part":"p07","title":"A summer job at a call center","level":"A2","words":["call center","telecom","script","operator","billing","service center","clerk","back office","fax","vending"],"story":"This summer Anna works at a [[call center]]. It belongs to a big [[telecom]] company. Every morning she reads her answers from a [[script]]. Difficult calls go to an [[operator]] with more experience. Questions about bills go to [[billing]]. Angry clients with broken phones go to the [[service center]]. One day Anna needs an old contract. A [[clerk]] named Mr. Bondar brings it from the [[back office]]. He still sends documents by [[fax]]! Anna laughs, and he laughs too. At lunch they buy snacks from the [[vending]] machine together."},{"id":"c064","part":"p07","title":"A problem at work","level":"B1","words":["harassment","dilemma","conflict","tact","guideline","compliance","compliance officer","ultimatum"],"story":"One evening, Max's colleague Olena tells him about [[harassment]] by their manager, Mr. Shevchuk. Max faces a [[dilemma]]: he wants to help, but he is new on the team. He does not want an open [[conflict]], so he decides to act with [[tact]]. First, he reads the company [[guideline]] about [[compliance]] and workplace behavior. Then Olena and Max talk to the [[compliance officer]] together. She listens carefully and takes notes. A week later, the director gives Mr. Shevchuk an [[ultimatum]]: change or leave. He leaves, and his loyal lackey, who always laughed at his jokes, leaves too. Now Olena feels safe at work again."},{"id":"c065","part":"p07","title":"Big changes at the company","level":"B1","words":["top management","business case","business process","middle management","resource","management","sector","motive","process"],"story":"Anna's aunt Iryna works at a big delivery company. One day [[top management]] announces big changes. They write a [[business case]] for a new way of working. Every [[business process]] in the company must change. They also cut [[middle management]] to save [[resources|resource]]. Aunt Iryna has worked in [[management]] in this [[sector]] for fifteen years. She is not happy about the changes. At dinner, Anna asks about her [[motive]] for leaving the company. \"I want to choose my own projects,\" Aunt Iryna explains. Leaving is a long [[process]], with many papers and meetings. But after two months, she starts freelance work from home, and she loves it."},{"id":"c066","part":"p08","title":"Professor Brown's class","level":"A1","words":["class","semester","professor","old-school","syllabus","curriculum","marker","attribute","campus","institute","college"],"story":"It is Anna's first [[class]] this [[semester]]. Her teacher is [[Professor|professor]] Brown. He has an [[old-school]] way of teaching. He gives everyone a paper [[syllabus]]. It shows the [[curriculum]] for the year. He writes on the board with a [[marker]]. \"Patience is an important [[attribute]],\" he says. Then he shows them the [[campus]]. They walk to the old [[institute]] building. \"It was a small [[college]] before,\" he says. Anna wants to be patient too."},{"id":"c067","part":"p08","title":"Anna's English test","level":"A1","words":["test","text","dialogue","essay","adjective","synonym","context","equivalent","comma","consonant"],"story":"Anna takes an English course at the university. Today she has a big [[test]]. It takes a minimum of two hours. First, she reads a [[text]] and writes a [[dialogue]]. Then she writes an [[essay]] about Kyiv. She chooses the right [[adjective]] and a [[synonym]]. The [[context]] helps her find each Ukrainian [[equivalent]]. Later, the teacher shows her two small mistakes. She forgets a [[comma]] and a [[consonant]]. But she still gets a good grade!"},{"id":"c068","part":"p08","title":"Small talk with exchange students","level":"A2","words":["Hindi","small talk","barrier","accent","slang","dialect","sarcasm","cliché","acronym","euphemism","nuance","stereotype"],"story":"Anna meets three exchange students from India, Ireland and Texas. Priya from India also speaks [[Hindi]]. At first, [[small talk]] is hard for Anna. There is a language [[barrier]], and everyone has a different [[accent]]. Liam uses a lot of [[slang]], and Jake speaks a southern [[dialect]]. When Jake says \"Great weather!\" in the rain, it is [[sarcasm]]. Liam laughs and says \"Time flies,\" a famous [[cliché]]. Priya writes \"LOL\" in the chat, and Anna learns a new [[acronym]]. Liam's cousin is \"between jobs,\" a polite [[euphemism]] for no work. Anna understands that every word can carry a [[nuance]]. \"Not every Texan rides a horse,\" Jake says. \"That is a [[stereotype]]!\" By the end of the evening, they are good friends."},{"id":"c069","part":"p08","title":"Taras's math homework","level":"A2","words":["algebra","method","calculator","formula","radius","perimeter","cube","cylinder","oval","spiral"],"story":"Anna's little brother Taras has [[algebra]] homework from Mrs. Koval. He is sad because it looks very hard. Anna shows him an easy [[method]]. First, they take a [[calculator]] from the drawer. They use a [[formula]] with pi. With it, they find the [[radius]] of a circle. Next, they find the [[perimeter]] of a square. After that, Taras draws a [[cube]], a [[cylinder]] and an [[oval]]. On the last page, he draws a big [[spiral]] just for fun. \"Math is fun with you!\" he says. The next day, he gets a top grade."},{"id":"c070","part":"p08","title":"Anna studies online","level":"A2","words":["online course","streak","tutorial","module","e-learning","portal","certificate","grant","course"],"story":"Anna is taking an [[online course]] in marketing. Her learning app shows a thirty-day [[streak]], and she is proud. Every evening she watches a video [[tutorial]]. Each [[module]] of the [[e-learning]] program has a short quiz. For hard topics, she books one-to-one lessons on the student [[portal]]. After six weeks, she gets a [[certificate]]! Her teacher says, \"You should apply for a [[grant]].\" With that money, she can take a longer [[course]] at the university. Anna fills in the form that same night."},{"id":"c071","part":"p08","title":"A day in the library","level":"A2","words":["archive","encyclopedia","atlas","manuscript","Latin","paperback","fiction","author","pseudonym","prologue"],"story":"On Saturday, Anna spends the whole day in the old university library. First, she visits its [[archive]] in the basement. She finds a huge [[encyclopedia]] and an old [[atlas]] of the world. She also finds an old [[manuscript]] in [[Latin]]. Anna cannot read it, but she takes a picture. Later, she sits by the window with a [[paperback]]. It is [[fiction]], a mystery about a lost ship. The [[author]] writes under a [[pseudonym]]. In the [[prologue]], the writer explains how the story began. Anna reads until the library closes."},{"id":"c072","part":"p08","title":"Trouble at Taras's school","level":"A2","words":["prank","geek","loser","IQ","hater","bullying","nerve"],"story":"Some older boys at school play a cruel [[prank]] on Taras. They hide his bag and laugh at him. They call him a [[geek]] and a [[loser]] for his high [[IQ]]. Then a [[hater]] writes mean comments about him online. The [[bullying]] really gets on his [[nerves|nerve]]. Soon Taras has a nervous tic in his eye. Anna talks to his teacher about the problem. The school gives Taras a mentor, a kind older student named Dmytro. They talk every week, and Taras feels strong again."},{"id":"c073","part":"p08","title":"Aunt Iryna's Doctorate","level":"B1","words":["doctorate","alma mater","argument","discourse","ergo","prestige","intellectual","intellect"],"story":"Anna's aunt Iryna finally finished her [[doctorate]] in sociology this fall. In October, Anna went with her to her [[alma mater]] in Lviv. The university held a big symposium there, and Iryna gave the opening talk. Her main [[argument]] was simple: public [[discourse]] online is getting too angry. \"People stop listening; [[ergo]], they stop learning,\" she said. After the talk, the dean asked her to help write a new curriculum on media. Iryna enjoyed the [[prestige]] of the invitation, but she was happiest about the work. On the train home, Anna called her a real [[intellectual]]. \"You have a great [[intellect]], Aunt Iryna!\" she said. Iryna laughed. \"No, I just read a lot of books.\""},{"id":"f02","part":"p08","title":"Measuring everything at home","level":"A2","words":["kilo","kilogram","gram","milligram","liter","meter","kilometer","millimeter"],"story":"Taras has a school project: measure everything at home. Anna helps him with the kitchen scale. A bag of sugar weighs one [[kilo]]. \"A kilo is short for a [[kilogram]],\" Anna explains. One spoon of salt weighs only ten [[grams|gram]]. Mom's vitamin pill has just fifty [[milligrams|milligram]] of iron. Next, they fill a big bottle with one [[liter]] of water. The kitchen table is almost two [[meters|meter]] long. Their walk to school is about one [[kilometer]]. Last, Taras measures an ant: just three [[millimeters|millimeter]]! His teacher loves the project and gives him a gold star."},{"id":"c074","part":"p09","title":"Anna Has a Virus","level":"A1","words":["doctor","pulse","thermometer","symptom","aspirin","effect"],"story":"Anna feels bad today, so she visits the [[doctor]]. The doctor checks her [[pulse]]. Then she uses a [[thermometer]]. It says 38 degrees! She asks Anna about her [[symptoms|symptom]]. Anna has a headache and a sore throat. \"It is a virus,\" the doctor says. \"You do not need an antibiotic. Take an [[aspirin]], 500 milligrams, twice a day.\" The next morning, Anna feels much better. The medicine has a good [[effect]]."},{"id":"c075","part":"p09","title":"Max at the Clinic","level":"A2","words":["front office","implant","floss","retainer","acne","retina","laser"],"story":"Max has a busy morning at the city clinic. First, he checks in at the [[front office]]. His tooth hurts, so the dentist gives him an anesthetic. \"You may need an [[implant]] one day,\" she says. She also tells him to use [[floss]] every night. \"And wear your [[retainer]], please!\" Next, a skin doctor checks his [[acne]] and gives him a cream. Finally, an eye doctor looks at his [[retina]]. \"Your eyes are fine. You don't need [[laser]] surgery,\" she says. Max leaves the clinic tired but happy."},{"id":"c076","part":"p09","title":"Dad's Yearly Checkup","level":"A2","words":["checkup","cholesterol","risk factor","stress test","screening","specialist","migraine","case management","pacemaker"],"story":"Anna's dad has his yearly [[checkup]] on Monday. The doctor says his [[cholesterol]] is a little high. She asks about his [[risk factors|risk factor]], like smoking and stress. She sends him for a [[stress test]] and a cancer [[screening]]. She also wants him to see a heart [[specialist]]. \"Do you still get [[migraines|migraine]]?\" she asks. \"Only on Mondays,\" Dad jokes. The clinic's [[case management]] team also helps Grandpa. They check his [[pacemaker]] and his insulin. They also look at the tremor in his hands. In the evening, Dad and Grandpa eat a healthy salad together."},{"id":"c077","part":"p09","title":"Anna's Healthy Lifestyle","level":"A2","words":["lifestyle","vitamin","omega-3","yoga","electrolyte","detox","metabolism","wellness","anti-aging"],"story":"This year, Anna wants a healthier [[lifestyle]]. First, she stops eating junk food after classes. She buys [[vitamins|vitamin]] and fish oil with [[omega-3]]. Every morning, she puts bananas and milk in the blender. She drinks a big smoothie before class. After [[yoga]], she has a drink with [[electrolytes|electrolyte]]. On the weekend, she even tries a juice [[detox]]. In the evenings, she reads about [[metabolism]] and [[wellness]] online. At last, she shows Max a new [[anti-aging]] cream. \"Anna, you are nineteen!\" Max laughs. \"Okay, maybe I don't need this one,\" Anna says with a smile."},{"id":"c078","part":"p09","title":"Talking About Stress","level":"B1","words":["stress","discomfort","trigger","phobia","coping","mindset","optimism","self-help","stress management","stigma","suicide","self-harm"],"story":"Before her exams, Anna is under a lot of [[stress]]. Some nights she feels [[discomfort]] in her chest and cannot sleep. Max tells her to visit the college counselor, a kind woman named Olena. Olena asks Anna to write down every [[trigger]] that makes her anxious. They also talk about Anna's [[phobia]] of speaking in front of big groups. Olena teaches her simple [[coping]] skills, like slow breathing and short walks. \"A calm, positive [[mindset]] really helps,\" she says, \"and so does a little [[optimism]].\" She gives Anna a [[self-help]] book and a weekly [[stress management]] plan. Asking for help is brave, she says, even with the [[stigma]] around mental health. Later that week, she gives every student a hotline number for thoughts of [[suicide]] or [[self-harm]]. Anna passes her exams, and she keeps the book on her desk."},{"id":"c079","part":"p09","title":"Grandma Remembers Lockdown","level":"A2","words":["COVID","lockdown","influenza","pneumonia","monitoring","quarantine","booster"],"story":"On a rainy evening, Anna asks Grandma about the [[COVID]] years. \"The whole city was in [[lockdown]] for weeks,\" Grandma says. \"A virus is a kind of pathogen, so we all stayed home. In winter, [[influenza]] was dangerous too. Your grandpa got [[pneumonia]] and went to the hospital. He needed oxygen and careful [[monitoring]] for five days. I stayed in [[quarantine]] at home and called him every day. Later, we both got a [[booster]] shot.\" Anna hugs her. \"I'm glad those days are over, Grandma.\""},{"id":"c080","part":"p09","title":"An accident in the street","level":"A2","words":["dispatcher","paramedic","shock","trauma","morphine","pager","coma","donor","distress","medic"],"story":"On Monday, Anna sees a man fall off his bike. She calls for help, and the [[dispatcher]] sends an ambulance. Soon a [[paramedic]] named Olha arrives. The man is in [[shock]] and has head [[trauma]]. Olha gives him [[morphine]] for the pain. At the hospital, a doctor's [[pager]] beeps, and she runs to him. The man is in a [[coma]] for one day. He needs blood from a [[donor]]. His wife is in great [[distress]], so Anna stays with her. Later, Anna's cousin Ira, an army [[medic]], brings them hot tea. The next evening, the man wakes up and smiles at them."},{"id":"c081","part":"p09","title":"Health Week at College","level":"B1","words":["penis","vagina","hormone","libido","orgasm","condom","tampon","herpes","syphilis","porno"],"story":"During health week, Dr. Kovalenko visits Anna's college to give a sex education class. She shows a clear diagram of the [[penis]] and the [[vagina]] and explains how they work. Then she explains how a [[hormone]] like testosterone can change your mood and body. Stress and poor sleep can lower your [[libido]], she says. She also explains what an [[orgasm]] is, in calm, scientific words. Next, she shows how to use a [[condom]] correctly to stay safe. She tells the students that a [[tampon]] is safe if you change it often. Infections like [[herpes]] and [[syphilis]] are common, but doctors can test for them and help. Finally, she says that [[porno]] is not real life and gives a wrong picture of love. Nobody laughs, and many students stay after class to ask questions. Max says it is the most useful class of the year."},{"id":"c082","part":"p09","title":"Uncle Petro's way back","level":"B1","words":["alcoholic","alcoholism","rehab","nicotine","heroin","opiate","opium","cocaine","meth","marijuana","LSD","cannabis","ganja","amphetamine","methadone"],"story":"Anna's uncle Petro is an [[alcoholic]], and the family has worried about him for years. Last spring, after a long fight with [[alcoholism]], he finally went to [[rehab]]. He also stopped smoking, because he did not want [[nicotine]] to control him too. In his support group, one woman used [[heroin]] and other [[opiates|opiate]] for ten years. The group leader explains that these drugs all come from [[opium]], which is made from poppies. A young man talks about [[cocaine]] and [[meth]] and the friends he lost. Another man started with [[marijuana]] at parties and later tried [[LSD]]. He says [[cannabis]] is the plant's proper name, but his friends just called it [[ganja]]. A woman explains how [[amphetamine]] pills ruined her sleep and her job. An older man takes [[methadone]] every day to stay away from street drugs. Petro listens to everyone and feels less alone. On Sunday, he drinks only tea at family dinner, and Anna hugs him."},{"id":"c083","part":"p10","title":"The big match on TV","level":"A2","words":["fan","football","fanatic","derby","match","versus","referee","foul","offside","goalkeeper","extra time","midfielder","winger","goal","replay"],"story":"Max is a [[fan]] of the Kyiv Reds. But his dad is a real [[football]] [[fanatic]]. Tonight, they watch the city [[derby]] on TV together. The [[match]] is Kyiv Reds [[versus]] Kyiv Blues. In the first half, the [[referee]] calls a [[foul]] on the Reds. Later, he calls an [[offside]], and Dad shouts at the TV. In the second half, the Reds' [[goalkeeper]] saves a penalty. It is 1-1, so the game goes into [[extra time]]. In the last minute, a [[midfielder]] passes to the fast [[winger]]. He scores the winning [[goal]]! Max and his dad jump up and watch the [[replay]] five times."},{"id":"c084","part":"p10","title":"Max at the gym","level":"A2","words":["sport","club","fitness center","trainer","guru","fitness","cardio","stretching","pilates","instructor","biceps","six-pack","mentor"],"story":"Max wants to do more [[sport]] this year. He joins a [[club]] with a big [[fitness center]]. His [[trainer]], Oleh, is a [[guru]] with many online followers. Oleh makes a plan to improve Max's [[fitness]]. Max does twenty minutes of [[cardio]] and some [[stretching]]. On Fridays, he goes to a [[pilates]] class with a kind [[instructor]]. One day, an older man shows Max his huge [[biceps]] and [[six-pack]]. \"I take special pills for big muscles,\" he says. \"No, thanks, I want to stay healthy,\" Max answers. Oleh hears this and becomes a real [[mentor]] to Max. After the workout, Max books a long massage."},{"id":"c085","part":"p10","title":"The Kyiv marathon","level":"A2","words":["jogging","tracker","start","runner","sprint","cross-country","triathlon","athlete","podium","medal","prize","medalist","doping","steroid"],"story":"Anna loves [[jogging]] in the park every morning. She checks her speed on her new fitness [[tracker]]. In May, she runs her first race in Kyiv. At the [[start]], she feels nervous but happy. Fast [[runners|runner]] go past her in a quick [[sprint]]. Max says some of them do [[cross-country]] and [[triathlon]] too. Anna runs slowly, but she does not stop. At the end, a young woman from Lviv wins the race. This strong [[athlete]] stands on the [[podium]]. She gets a gold [[medal]] and a big [[prize]]. Journalists ask another [[medalist]] about [[doping]] and [[steroids|steroid]]. Anna has no medal, but she is very proud."},{"id":"c086","part":"p10","title":"Taras learns karate","level":"A2","words":["karate","dojo","sensei","dan","kung fu","senpai","sparring","sumo","gymnast"],"story":"Taras is Anna's little brother, and he starts [[karate]] this month. His [[dojo]] is near his school. His [[sensei]] has a black belt and a fifth [[dan]]. She also teaches [[kung fu]] on weekends. An older boy, Roman, is Taras's [[senpai]] and helps him with kicks. Every Friday, the kids do [[sparring]] in pairs. At home, Taras watches [[sumo]] on TV with Dad. One day, he meets a young [[gymnast]] from the next hall. She can do a perfect split, and Taras wants to try. Now he practices kicks and splits every day."},{"id":"c087","part":"p10","title":"Boxing night","level":"B1","words":["boxer","MMA","challenger","underdog","fight","fighter","comeback","champ","knockout","commentator","champion","euphoria","highlight"],"story":"On Saturday night, Max invites his friends over to watch sports on TV. First they see a famous [[boxer]] win easily, and then the [[MMA]] event begins. The young [[challenger]] is clearly the [[underdog]], and nobody expects him to win. The main [[fight]] starts badly for him, and he falls in the first round. But this [[fighter]] does not give up, and slowly he makes a [[comeback]]. In the third round, he hits the [[champ]] hard and wins by [[knockout]]. The [[commentator]] screams, \"We have a new [[champion]]!\" and Max's cat hides. The fans in the hall are in total [[euphoria]], and so are Max's friends. Later, they watch the [[highlights|highlight]] again and again until midnight. Max says, \"Tomorrow I'm going to the gym!\""},{"id":"c088","part":"p10","title":"Basketball After School","level":"A2","words":["basketball","roster","playoff","opponent","teammate","dunk","rebound","assist","time-out","final","triumph","mascot","fair play"],"story":"Taras plays [[basketball]] for his school team. One Monday, the coach shows the [[roster]] for the next game. Taras sees his name on it and smiles. It is a [[playoff]] game against a strong [[opponent]]. In the first half, a [[teammate]] makes a great [[dunk]]. Then Taras gets the [[rebound]] and makes an [[assist]]. The other team scores fast, so the coach calls a [[time-out]]. After that, Taras's team plays better and wins. Next week, they also win the [[final]]! It is a real [[triumph]] for the whole school. The school [[mascot]], a big blue bear, dances on the court. Both teams shake hands, because the coach loves [[fair play]]."},{"id":"c089","part":"p10","title":"A day at the sea","level":"A2","words":["ocean","surfing","SUP","surfer","fiberglass","surfboard","kayak","diving","diver","keel","buoy","skydiving","canoe"],"story":"Max and Anna spend their summer vacation by the [[ocean]]. On the first day, they try [[surfing]] and [[SUP]]. A friendly [[surfer]] shows them his light [[fiberglass]] [[surfboard]]. Then they rent a [[kayak]] for two hours. The next morning, they go [[diving]] with a [[diver]] named Oleh. From the water, they see a small boat near the shore. Its [[keel]] hits a [[buoy]], but nobody is hurt. Above the beach, people are [[skydiving]] with colorful parachutes. In the evening, they race in a [[canoe]] along the shore. Anna wins, and Max says she is just lucky. Tired and happy, they eat ice cream and watch the sunset."},{"id":"c090","part":"p10","title":"Boards and Bikes","level":"A2","words":["skateboarding","skateboard","composite","trail","snowboarding","hockey","frisbee","paintball","bowling"],"story":"Taras and his friends love extreme sports and hip-hop. After school, they go [[skateboarding]] in the park. Taras rides a new [[skateboard]] from his grandma. On Saturday, they take their mountain bikes to the forest. The bikes have light [[composite]] frames. They ride on a long [[trail]] near the river. Taras loves biking, but in winter he prefers [[snowboarding]]. His friends also play [[hockey]], [[frisbee]] and [[paintball]]. One evening, they invite Anna to join them. Anna laughs and says, \"I want something calm.\" So everyone goes [[bowling]], and Anna wins every game!"},{"id":"c091","part":"p10","title":"An American Sports Weekend","level":"B1","words":["baseball","inning","home run","quarterback","linebacker","touchdown","field goal","cheerleader","cheerleading","rodeo","lacrosse","softball"],"story":"In October, Max flies to Texas to visit his friend Jake. On Friday night, they watch [[baseball]] at a small local stadium. In the last [[inning]], a young player hits a [[home run]], and everyone jumps up. On Saturday, Jake takes him to an American football game at his old high school. The [[quarterback]] throws the ball far, and a big [[linebacker]] falls on the grass. Then the home team scores a [[touchdown]] and later a [[field goal]]. The [[cheerleaders|cheerleader]] dance and jump, and Max finds their [[cheerleading]] amazing. On Sunday, they go to a [[rodeo]], where cowboys ride wild horses. After that, they watch Jake's sister play [[lacrosse]] in the park. Her friends invite Max to try [[softball]], and he misses every ball. Max laughs and says that sports at home feel much easier."},{"id":"c092","part":"p10","title":"Golf with Uncle Victor","level":"B1","words":["golf club","golf","caddie","tennis","grand slam","polo","rugby","cricket","bowler","badminton","ping-pong","volleyball"],"story":"Max's rich uncle Victor invites him to his [[golf club]] on Sunday. Max has never played [[golf]], so he feels a little nervous. A friendly [[caddie]] carries their heavy bags across the green grass. While they walk, Uncle Victor talks about [[tennis]] and his trip to a [[grand slam]] final. He also loves [[polo]], [[rugby]] and especially [[cricket]]. He explains that in that game a [[bowler]] throws the ball at the wickets. Max tries his first shot, but the ball flies straight into the lake. Everyone laughs, including Max himself. On the way home, Max says, \"Next time, let's just play [[badminton]] in the yard.\" Uncle Victor smiles and says, \"Or [[ping-pong]] in my basement, or [[volleyball]] on the beach.\""},{"id":"c093","part":"p11","title":"Max's band","level":"A2","words":["bass","band","drummer","rhythm","guitarist","instrument","frontman","vocalist","tone","demo"],"story":"Max loves rock, and he plays [[bass]] in a [[band]] with friends. This month, they want to try heavy metal. Every evening, they practice in Max's garage. The [[drummer]], Ihor, keeps a fast [[rhythm]]. The [[guitarist]], Sofia, tunes her [[instrument]] very carefully. Their [[frontman]], Dima, talks to the crowd at every show. As the [[vocalist]], he cannot find the right [[tone]] for one song. He tries again and again, and finally it sounds great. On Sunday, they record their first [[demo]] on a phone. Max sends it to Anna, and she says it's loud but cool."},{"id":"c094","part":"p11","title":"Concert night","level":"A1","words":["concert","arena","sold out","intro","album","vocal","groupie","tour manager","merch","merchandising","live show"],"story":"Anna and Max go to a [[concert]] tonight. It is at the new [[arena]] in Kyiv. All the tickets are [[sold out]]. But Max has two premium tickets! The band starts with a long [[intro]]. Then they play a song from the new [[album]]. The singer has very strong [[vocals|vocal]]. A happy [[groupie]] sings every word. Anna sees the [[tour manager]] near the stage. At the end, Max buys [[merch]] for his sister. She works in [[merchandising]] at a clothing store. Anna says, \"I love a good [[live show]]!\""},{"id":"c095","part":"p11","title":"A summer music festival","level":"A2","words":["festival","fest","lineup","hip-hop","rap","R&B","reggae","rapper","freestyle","MC","fiesta"],"story":"In July, Anna and Max go to a summer music [[festival]]. Max just calls it \"the [[fest]].\" The [[lineup]] has something for everyone. There is [[hip-hop]], [[rap]], [[R&B]], [[reggae]] and electro. First, a young [[rapper]] does a [[freestyle]] with the [[MC]]. The crowd shouts and claps to the beat. Anna does not know any of the songs. But by the evening, she has five new favorites. At night, the park feels like a big [[fiesta]], with dancing everywhere. On the way home, Anna plays her new songs on her phone."},{"id":"c096","part":"p11","title":"Jazz in a Small Club","level":"A2","words":["jazz","blues","pianist","funk","unison","groove","jukebox"],"story":"On Friday, Anna's dad takes her to a small [[jazz]] club. It is warm and dark, and it smells of coffee. First, a trio plays the [[blues]]. Then a [[pianist]] plays a happy [[funk]] song. An old man plays the saxophone with his eyes closed. A young woman plays the bongos next to him. At the end, the band plays the last line in [[unison]]. The music has a great [[groove]], and Anna taps her feet. In the corner, she sees an old [[jukebox]]. Dad puts in a coin, and they dance to one more song."},{"id":"c097","part":"p11","title":"A night at the opera","level":"B1","words":["opera","quartet","sonata","trio","duo","phantom","soprano","aria","solo","tenor","duet","maestro","ensemble"],"story":"Grandma Halyna buys two tickets to the [[opera]] for Anna's birthday. Before the show, a string [[quartet]] plays a gentle [[sonata]] in the big hall. In the lobby, a small jazz [[trio]] plays for the people waiting. Grandma jokes that she and Anna are a funny [[duo]], like on TV. The story is about a sad [[phantom]] who lives under an old theater. A young [[soprano]] steps forward and sings a beautiful [[aria]] about love. It is a [[solo]], so she stands alone in the bright light. Then a [[tenor]] answers her, and they sing a [[duet]] with warm voices. The [[maestro]] smiles and leads the whole [[ensemble]] into the final song. At the end, Anna claps so hard that her hands hurt. \"Next year, I'm buying the tickets,\" she tells Grandma."},{"id":"c098","part":"p11","title":"Taras's music lesson","level":"A2","words":["fa","la","interval","trombone","tuba","piccolo","sax","saxophone","banjo","ukulele","bongo","gong"],"story":"Taras plays in the school band. Today his teacher sings two notes, [[fa]] and [[la]]. \"The space between two notes is an [[interval]],\" she says. Taras plays the [[trombone]], and his friend Ihor plays the [[tuba]]. A small girl plays the [[piccolo]] very high. Ihor's brother plays [[sax]] in the back. \"Sax is just short for [[saxophone]],\" he tells a new boy. The new boy has a [[banjo]], and his sister has a [[ukulele]]. Another boy plays the [[bongos|bongo]] with his hands. At the end, the teacher hits a big [[gong]]. Everyone laughs, and the lesson is over."},{"id":"c099","part":"p11","title":"Dance lessons","level":"A2","words":["tango","salsa","samba","carnival","polka","boogie","ballet","ballerina","waltz","mambo"],"story":"Anna and Max take dance lessons before cousin Olya's wedding. On Monday, they learn the [[tango]]. Max steps on Anna's foot twice. On Wednesday, they dance [[salsa]] and then [[samba]]. \"We can dance this at the [[carnival]] in February!\" says Anna. On Friday, the teacher shows them a fast [[polka]]. Max likes the [[boogie]] best. After class, they watch a [[ballet]] on TV. \"A [[ballerina]] never steps on feet,\" Anna jokes. At the wedding, they dance a slow [[waltz]] first. Then they dance the [[mambo]] all night, and nobody falls."},{"id":"c100","part":"p11","title":"Dad's Old Records","level":"A2","words":["vinyl","CD","stereo","rock and roll","hard rock","heavy metal","rocker","punk","new wave","rock band","punk rock","hippie","revival","rock","era","disc","disk","retro"],"story":"On Sunday, Dad opens a box of [[vinyl]] records and [[CDs|CD]]. He plays them on his big [[stereo]]. First, they hear [[rock and roll]], then loud [[hard rock]]. Then comes [[heavy metal]], and Anna covers her ears. \"I was a [[rocker]] and loved [[punk]] and [[new wave]],\" Dad says. \"My [[rock band]] played fast [[punk rock]] in the garage.\" Grandpa was a [[hippie]] and played the banjo. \"Today there is a [[revival]] of old [[rock]],\" Dad says happily. \"It was a great [[era]].\" Then Dad finds a shiny [[disc]] with his band's songs. Anna saves the songs to the [[disk]] on her laptop. She puts on Dad's [[retro]] jacket and asks, \"Can I keep it?\""},{"id":"c101","part":"p11","title":"Max's First Rave","level":"B1","words":["rave","mega","techno","electro","acid house","goth","synth"],"story":"On Saturday night, Max goes to his first [[rave]] in an old factory. It is a [[mega]] party with hundreds of people and colorful lights. The DJ plays a long set that starts with fast [[techno]] and bright [[electro]]. Then the music turns into old [[acid house]], and everyone jumps. Next to Max, a quiet [[goth]] in black clothes plays a [[synth]] on a small stage. At sunrise, a band plays loud guitar music, and Max dances until his legs hurt. In the morning, he texts Anna: \"I need to sleep for two days!\""},{"id":"c102","part":"p11","title":"Sofia Writes a Song","level":"B1","words":["songwriter","folk","new age","world music","producer","instrumental","remix","mix","release","debut","title track","track"],"story":"Max's sister Sofia is a young [[songwriter]] who writes songs in her small room. She loves [[folk]], but she also listens to calm [[new age]] and [[world music]]. One day, a [[producer]] hears her songs and invites her to his studio. With her friend Oleh, she records a duet about the rain. He adds a long [[instrumental]] in the middle of the song. Later, a DJ makes a [[remix]] and plays it in his party [[mix]]. They plan the [[release]] of her [[debut]] album for May. The [[title track]] is a song about Kyiv at night. When the album comes out, the whole family listens to it together. Max says the last [[track]] is the best one."},{"id":"c103","part":"p11","title":"The School Play","level":"A2","words":["role","theater","drama","prince","protagonist","monologue","poet","sonnet","masquerade","actor","repertoire","artiste","talent"],"story":"Taras gets a big [[role]] in the school play. The show is at the city [[theater]] on Friday. The play is a [[drama]] about a lost kingdom. Taras plays a young [[prince]]. He is the [[protagonist]], so he has many lines. In the second act, he says a long [[monologue]]. In the next scene, a [[poet]] reads a [[sonnet]] at a [[masquerade]]. Before they start, every [[actor]] is nervous, but Taras is calm. Their teacher knows the whole school [[repertoire]] by heart. After the show, a famous [[artiste]] from the city shakes his hand. Then the teacher says, \"Taras, you have real [[talent]]!\""},{"id":"c104","part":"p11","title":"A Weekend of Comedy","level":"B1","words":["improv","stand-up","cabaret","drag queen","revue","musical","matinee","fail","music hall","humor","farce","fiasco"],"story":"On Friday, Anna and her friends start their comedy weekend with an [[improv]] show. After that, they see a short [[stand-up]] set by a nervous young comedian. On Saturday, they go to a [[cabaret]], where a [[drag queen]] welcomes everyone. The evening ends with a [[revue]] of songs from a famous [[musical]]. On Sunday, they buy cheap tickets for the [[matinee]] and laugh at a comedy duo. One joke about cats is a total [[fail]], but the two comedians laugh at it too. In the evening, they go to a charity gala at the old [[music hall]]. There, an old singer with great [[humor]] tells funny stories. The last act is a short [[farce]] about two lost brothers. Suddenly, the lights go out, and part of the stage falls down. \"What a [[fiasco]]!\" someone shouts, but everyone just laughs. At midnight, Max says, \"My face hurts from laughing!\""},{"id":"c105","part":"p11","title":"A day at the art museum","level":"A2","words":["art","renaissance","portrait","madonna","symbolism","contour","sculptor","pedestal","antique","realism","critic","art critic","curator","contrast"],"story":"On Saturday, Anna takes Max to the [[art]] museum. Max likes a [[Renaissance|renaissance]] [[portrait]] of a man in a red hat. Anna likes a painting of the [[Madonna|madonna]], full of [[symbolism]]. Then she studies the [[contour]] of a face in a drawing. Statues by a famous [[sculptor]] stand on stone [[pedestals|pedestal]]. Max wants to sit on a chair, but it is an [[antique]]! Upstairs, there are modern paintings in the style of [[realism]]. \"That man is a movie [[critic]] from TV,\" Anna whispers. \"The woman next to him is an [[art critic]].\" The [[curator]] shows them a big painting of Kyiv. She talks about its strong [[contrast]] of dark and light. Both critics smile, and Max takes a photo."},{"id":"c106","part":"p11","title":"Street art in Kyiv","level":"A2","words":["graffiti","mural","public art","facade","exterior","indigo","art space","contemporary art","avant-garde","illustrator","design","designer","visual"],"story":"In an old district of Kyiv, Max shows Anna walls with [[graffiti]]. On one house, there is a huge [[mural]] of a big bird. \"The city pays for this [[public art]],\" Max says. The [[facade]] is gray stone, but the bird is on the side. So the [[exterior]] of the house is gray, [[indigo]] and white. Next, they go into an [[art space]] in an old factory. It shows [[contemporary art]] by young artists. One room is full of [[avant-garde]] pictures. Anna buys a poster by a local [[illustrator]]. An old teacher talks about [[design]] with a young [[designer]]. She shows him a bright [[visual]] for a concert. At home, Anna puts her new poster on the wall."},{"id":"c107","part":"p12","title":"What shall we watch?","level":"A2","words":["film","streaming","streaming service","trailer","preview","promo","rating","genre","thriller","sci-fi","fantasy","spoiler","sequel","blockbuster","remake","spin-off"],"story":"On Friday, Anna and Max want to watch a [[film]] at home. Max says [[streaming]] is better than the cinema. They open their [[streaming service]], but they cannot choose. They watch two [[trailers|trailer]], a short [[preview]] and a loud [[promo]]. Anna checks every [[rating]], and they argue about the [[genre]]. Anna wants a [[thriller]], but Max wants [[sci-fi]]. \"What about [[fantasy]]?\" Anna asks. Then Max gives a [[spoiler]] about the [[sequel]] of a summer [[blockbuster]]. Anna throws a pillow at him. \"OK, a [[remake]] of an old comedy, then?\" Max asks. Finally, they choose a [[spin-off]] about a funny neighbor. They both laugh all evening."},{"id":"c108","part":"p12","title":"Max's favorite TV show","level":"A2","words":["prime time","show","episode","sitcom","game show","reality show","talk show","gag","segment","entertainment","talent show"],"story":"On Thursdays at [[prime time]], the family watches TV together. But everyone wants a different [[show]]. Max wants a new [[episode]] of his favorite [[sitcom]]. Grandma prefers a [[game show]] with big prizes. Taras loves a [[reality show]] about young cooks. Mom wants a [[talk show]] with a funny [[gag]] about a cat. Its next [[segment]] is about healthy food. Max sighs and says, \"We need better [[entertainment]]!\" Then Taras has an idea: a family [[talent show]] in the living room! Grandma sings, Mom dances, and Max tells jokes. Nobody turns on the TV all evening."},{"id":"c109","part":"p12","title":"A Day on Set","level":"B1","words":["casting","filmmaker","production designer","cameraman","close-up","narrator","setting","flashback","footage","suspense","soundtrack","cameo"],"story":"Sofia went to a [[casting]] and got a small role as an extra. On her first day, she met the young [[filmmaker]] and the [[production designer]]. The [[cameraman]] asked her to stand still for a [[close-up]] of her face. Between scenes, the [[narrator]] explained the [[setting]]: a small town in the 1960s. Sofia's scene was a [[flashback]] to the main character's childhood. In the evening, the director showed the team a short preview. The [[footage]] was full of [[suspense]], and the [[soundtrack]] was beautiful. Then Sofia laughed: the director had a tiny [[cameo]] as a bus driver beside her."},{"id":"c110","part":"p12","title":"Grandpa's Old Films","level":"B1","words":["drive-in","noir","melodrama","mainstream","indie","homage","negative","slide show","nostalgia"],"story":"On Sunday, Grandpa told Anna about the old [[drive-in]] near his village. Before that, he and Grandma often went to shows at the music hall downtown. His favorite movies are classic [[noir]], but Grandma always loved a good [[melodrama]]. \"I never liked the [[mainstream]],\" Grandpa said. \"I prefer [[indie]].\" He put a disc into the old player, and they watched a remake of a detective movie. \"It's a nice [[homage]] to the original,\" he said. Later, Anna found an old photo album and a box of [[negatives|negative]]. She scanned them and made a [[slide show]] for the whole family. When Grandpa saw it, his eyes were full of [[nostalgia]]."},{"id":"c111","part":"p12","title":"Taras's anime and manga","level":"A2","words":["anime","superman","kryptonite","minion","lackey","robot","droid","android","cyborg","creepy","vampire","cannibal","manga","saga"],"story":"Taras watches [[anime]] every night after dinner. His favorite hero is a shy boy at school. But at night, he is strong like a [[superman]]. His only weakness is cold water, his [[kryptonite]]. The villain has many [[minions|minion]] and one [[lackey]] who carries his coat. His [[robot]] cleans, his [[droid]] beeps, and his [[android]] looks human. His best fighter is a [[cyborg]], half man and half machine. They all live in a [[creepy]] castle with an old [[vampire]]. The castle cook is not a [[cannibal]]; he only makes soup! Before bed, Taras reads a [[manga]], a long [[saga]] about a hero. He falls asleep with the book on his face."},{"id":"c112","part":"p12","title":"Taras the Gamer","level":"A2","words":["gamer","gaming","console","controller","squad","item","combo","high score"],"story":"Taras is a real [[gamer]]. [[Gaming|gaming]] is his favorite hobby. On Saturday, he turns on his [[console]] and takes his new [[controller]]. He joins his online [[squad]]. Soon he finds a rare [[item]] and makes a ten-hit [[combo]]. Then the screen freezes. \"Lag again!\" he shouts. Dad checks the router and finds a problem with the IP address. The game restarts, and Taras loses his new [[high score]]. Dad smiles. \"Next time, buy faster internet, not a new add-on.\""},{"id":"c113","part":"p12","title":"Max makes a game","level":"B1","words":["game developer","project manager","dev","RPG","hobbit","elf","orc","goblin","ogre","mage","mana","gameplay","avatar"],"story":"Max and his friend Oleh dream of becoming [[game developers|game developer]]. This year, they finally start their own small project. Max's cousin Ira joins as [[project manager]], and a classmate joins as one more [[dev]]. Together they make an [[RPG]] about a magic forest. The hero is a small [[hobbit]] who travels with a brave [[elf]]. On the way, they fight an [[orc]], a sneaky [[goblin]] and a slow, angry [[ogre]]. Later they meet an old [[mage]] who has no [[mana]] left. The [[gameplay]] is simple, but their friends love it. Before the game starts, players choose their own [[avatar]]. After a month, a hundred people download the game, and Ira orders pizza for everyone."},{"id":"c114","part":"p12","title":"Uncle's poker night","level":"B1","words":["poker","joker","bluff","all-in","full house","hustler","casino","blackjack","gambling","jackpot","gambler","pinball"],"story":"Max's uncle Petro invites his friends for a [[poker]] night. They play with plastic chips, and in their house rules the [[joker]] can replace any card. Uncle Petro tries a big [[bluff]] and goes [[all-in]]. But his neighbor calmly shows a [[full house]]. \"You're a real [[hustler]]!\" Uncle Petro laughs and hands over all his chips. Then he tells long stories about a [[casino]] trip many years ago. He played [[blackjack]] all night and lost everything. \"[[Gambling|gambling]] is not for me anymore,\" he says. \"I never won a [[jackpot]], not once.\" Grandma shakes her head. \"You're a [[gambler]], Petro. Play [[pinball]] instead!\""},{"id":"c115","part":"p12","title":"Anna's Travel Blog","level":"A2","words":["blog","bio","hashtag","emoji","gif","tripod","content","comment","blogging","follower","blogger"],"story":"Anna starts a travel [[blog]] on the web. First, she writes a short [[bio]] about herself. Her first post is about a weekend in Lviv. She adds a [[hashtag]], a sun [[emoji]] and a funny [[gif]]. Max lends her his [[tripod]], and she films a short video clip. She works on her [[content]] every evening. She answers every [[comment]], even the short ones. After two months, [[blogging]] brings her a hundred [[followers|follower]]. Max smiles. \"Now you're a real [[blogger]]!\""},{"id":"c116","part":"p12","title":"Max goes viral","level":"A2","words":["video","video clip","clip","timeline","post","meme","trend","tag","tweet","hype","giveaway","how-to","hack","playlist"],"story":"Max films a funny [[video]] of his cat, Bublyk. It is long, so he cuts a short [[video clip]] from it. He drags the [[clip]] onto the [[timeline]] and adds music. Then he shares it in a [[post]] online. The next day, it is a [[meme]] and a city [[trend]]. People add a [[tag]] with the cat's name. His classmate writes a [[tweet]] about it. The [[hype]] grows every day. A pet shop offers a [[giveaway]] for his fans. Then Max shares a [[how-to]] about a kitchen [[hack]] for cat owners. He also makes a [[playlist]] of songs for cat lovers. Bublyk does not care and just sleeps on the keyboard."},{"id":"c117","part":"p12","title":"Trouble in the Comments","level":"B1","words":["troll","request","moderator","forum","trolling","hate speech","community","proof","info","fake news"],"story":"One evening, a [[troll]] wrote rude comments under Anna's post about Kyiv. Then he sent her a friend [[request]], which was very strange. Anna wrote to the [[moderator]] of the travel [[forum]]. She quickly stopped the [[trolling]] and deleted all the [[hate speech]]. The whole online [[community]] supported Anna. Then the rude user said that the Kyiv metro was closed for a year. People asked him for [[proof]] and real [[info]]. Of course, he had none, because it was just [[fake news]]. He disappeared that night, and Anna went back to planning her next trip."},{"id":"c118","part":"p12","title":"Anna's Podcast","level":"A2","words":["podcast","jingle","audio","recorder","audio file","booklet","storytelling","radio","interview","radio show"],"story":"Anna and Max start a [[podcast]] about student life in Kyiv. Max writes a short, happy [[jingle]] for the start. They record the [[audio]] on an old [[recorder]]. In the evening, Anna edits the [[audio file]] on her laptop. They also print a small [[booklet]] about the show. Every week they practice [[storytelling]] with funny stories from class. One day, a reporter from a local [[radio]] station calls them. She wants an [[interview]] with them on her [[radio show]]. Max is nervous, but Anna says, \"Just tell a good story!\""},{"id":"c119","part":"p12","title":"Meeting a superstar","level":"A2","words":["finalist","scout","show business","showbiz","celebrity","superstar","playboy","bodyguard","VIP","glamour","paparazzi","fan club","autograph"],"story":"Sofia is a [[finalist]] in a TV talent show. After her song, a talent [[scout]] gives her a card. \"I work in [[show business]],\" he says. \"People call it [[showbiz]] for short.\" Backstage, Sofia sees a real [[celebrity]]. He is a famous [[superstar]] and a rich [[playboy]]. A big [[bodyguard]] stands next to him. [[VIP]] guests talk about [[glamour]] and fast cars. Outside, the [[paparazzi]] take hundreds of photos. Then girls from her school [[fan club]] run to Sofia. They ask for her [[autograph]], not his!"},{"id":"c120","part":"p13","title":"A day at the zoo","level":"A2","words":["tiger","gorilla","orangutan","gibbon","primate","panda","zebra","leopard","crocodile","alligator","caiman","python","flamingo","lemur","habitat","snack bar"],"story":"On Saturday, Anna takes her little brother Taras to the zoo. First, they see a big [[tiger]] and a quiet [[gorilla]]. A mother [[orangutan]] holds her baby, and a [[gibbon]] swings above them. \"They are all [[primates|primate]], like us,\" Anna says. The [[panda]] eats bamboo, and a [[zebra]] runs in the sun. A [[leopard]] sleeps on a high branch. Next, a [[crocodile]], an [[alligator]] and a [[caiman]] lie in the water. Taras hides behind Anna when he sees the [[python]]. Then they watch pink [[flamingos|flamingo]] and funny [[lemurs|lemur]]. A guide explains each animal's natural [[habitat]]. At the end, they buy hot dogs at the [[snack bar]]."},{"id":"c121","part":"p13","title":"Dogs in the park","level":"A2","words":["picnic","pavilion","bulldog","beagle","basset","chihuahua","terrier","poodle","husky","collie","pit bull","instinct","parasite","excrement"],"story":"On Sunday, Anna's family has a [[picnic]] in the park. They sit at a table in the old [[pavilion]]. A [[bulldog]], a [[beagle]] and a sleepy [[basset]] want their sandwiches. A lady walks by with a tiny [[chihuahua]] in her bag. Behind her, a small [[terrier]] barks at a white [[poodle]]. Max arrives with his [[husky]] and his aunt's [[collie]]. A friendly [[pit bull]] plays with a ball near the trees. Max's aunt's dog moves the others together by [[instinct]], like sheep. A vet tells them about a [[parasite]] from dirty pond water. So Anna's dad fills a clean bowl for the dogs. Before they go home, Max cleans up his dog's [[excrement]]. Everyone says the park looks nicer than before."},{"id":"c122","part":"p13","title":"Grandma's farm","level":"A2","words":["farmer","tractor","hectare","acre","mule","bushel","homestead","gallon","nectar","pesticide","insecticide","hybrid"],"story":"Anna and Max spend Saturday on Grandma's farm. The [[farmer]] next door waves to them from his field. He drives his big [[tractor]] over forty [[hectares|hectare]] of wheat. 'In America, that's about a hundred [[acres|acre]],' says Max. Grandma's old [[mule]] is slow, but very strong. It carries ten [[bushels|bushel]] of apples from the [[homestead]] to the road. Max brings the mule a [[gallon]] of water from the well. Behind the house, bees collect [[nectar]] from the flowers. Grandma never uses a [[pesticide]] in her garden. 'An [[insecticide]] kills bees too, and bees are my friends,' she says. Her new tree is a [[hybrid]] of a pear and an apple. 'I want to taste the first fruit!' says Max."},{"id":"c123","part":"p13","title":"Hiking in the Carpathians","level":"A2","words":["hiking","camp","cliff","compass","peak","breeze","canyon","cedar","granite","plateau","flora","fauna","quartz","scouting","panorama"],"story":"In July, Anna and Max go [[hiking]] in the Carpathian Mountains. They stay at a small [[camp]] near a high [[cliff]]. Max uses a [[compass]] to find the path to the [[peak]]. On the way, a cool [[breeze]] comes up from the [[canyon]]. They rest under an old [[cedar]] on big [[granite]] rocks. Higher up, they walk across a wide, green [[plateau]]. Anna photographs the local [[flora]] and [[fauna]]: flowers, moss and birds. Then they paddle a canoe across a quiet mountain lake. On the shore, Max finds a shiny piece of [[quartz]]. Near the lake, they meet boy scouts who love [[scouting]]. Together they climb a hill and see a [[panorama]] of the mountains. Anna smiles, 'Let's come back next summer!'"},{"id":"c124","part":"p13","title":"National parks in America","level":"B1","words":["ranger","grizzly","coyote","raccoon","bison","gopher","caribou","mustang","cougar","puma","hickory"],"story":"In August, Anna and Max visit Max's cousin, a park [[ranger]] in America. On the first morning, he shows them a [[grizzly]] fishing in a cold river. At night a [[coyote]] howls, and by morning a [[raccoon]] is in their trash. Later, they drive slowly while a herd of [[bison]] crosses the road. Max laughs at a small [[gopher]] that pops out of a hole in the grass. Then they fly north to Alaska and watch [[caribou]] walk across the tundra. In Nevada, a group of wild [[mustangs|mustang]] runs across the dry plains. Their last stop is a swamp in Florida, where an alligator lies in the sun. Every evening, Max's cousin warns them to stay on the trail because of [[cougars|cougar]]. 'Some people call it a [[puma]], but it's the same big cat,' he says. On the last night, he makes a fire from [[hickory]] wood, and they roast corn. Anna says it was the best trip of her life."},{"id":"c125","part":"p13","title":"A Voyage at Sea","level":"B1","words":["voyage","orca","marlin","mackerel","pelican","albatross","coral","reef","plankton","hydra"],"story":"Anna's uncle Petro invites her on a two-week [[voyage]] on his small research ship. Before they leave the river port, an old fisherman shows them a huge carp. Out at sea, Anna stands on the deck and watches the water all day. Suddenly, an [[orca]] jumps out of the waves right next to the ship! A man on a fishing boat waves and holds up a giant [[marlin]]. That evening, the cook grills fresh [[mackerel]] for everyone on board. In the morning, a [[pelican]] dives and catches a fish in its big beak. For hours, a white [[albatross]] flies quietly above the ship. On the last day, a diver named Olha takes Anna to see living [[coral]]. The [[reef]] is full of colors, and the water is full of tiny [[plankton]]. Through a magnifying glass, Olha shows her a little [[hydra]]. That night, Anna writes in her diary: 'The sea is a whole world.'"},{"id":"c126","part":"p13","title":"A climate strike","level":"B1","words":["climate","smog","ozone","iceberg","methane","fracking","eco","tornado","cyclone","typhoon","tsunami","region"],"story":"On Friday, Anna joins a [[climate]] strike with other students in the park. Max's sign says, 'I want to see the sky, not [[smog]]!' A girl named Sofia talks about the [[ozone]] layer and a melting [[iceberg]] in the Arctic. A teacher explains that farm cows produce [[methane]], and cars produce carbon dioxide. Some students ask about [[fracking]] and the water under the ground. Anna shares simple [[eco]] ideas, like bikes and reusable bags. A boy says a [[tornado]] once damaged his grandma's house. Sofia explains that a [[cyclone]] is a giant spinning storm over warm ocean water. 'Near Asia, people call the same storm a [[typhoon]],' she adds. A [[tsunami]] is different: it's a huge wave after an earthquake under the sea. Any of them can hurt a whole [[region]] at once. In the end, the group cleans the park together and plants three small trees."},{"id":"c127","part":"p13","title":"At the natural history museum","level":"B1","words":["dinosaur","dodo","artifact","fragment","organism","chameleon","cocoon","termite","pheromone","magma","lava"],"story":"On Tuesday, Anna's little brother Taras visits the natural history museum with his class. First, they see a huge [[dinosaur]] and a [[dodo]], a bird that couldn't fly. In a glass case, they see a stone [[artifact]] and a [[fragment]] of mammoth bone. The guide says every living [[organism]] needs food, water and a home. In a warm tank, a [[chameleon]] slowly changes its color from green to brown. Taras finds a silk [[cocoon]] hanging on a small branch. Behind glass, [[termites|termite]] build a mud tower and follow a [[pheromone]] to find food. In the last hall, a model volcano shows red [[magma]] rising from deep underground. \"When it comes out of the volcano, we call it [[lava]],\" the guide explains. On the bus home, Taras says he wants to be a scientist."},{"id":"c128","part":"p14","title":"A weekend in Paris","level":"A2","words":["monsieur","madame","mademoiselle","madeleine","creme","brie","Herr","Frau","beret","chateau","a la"],"story":"On their weekend in Paris, Anna and Mama find a small bistro. The waiter says, \"Bonjour, [[monsieur]],\" to an old man. Then he smiles at Mama: \"Good afternoon, [[madame]].\" \"And for you, [[mademoiselle]]?\" he asks Anna. Anna orders a [[madeleine]] and [[creme]] brulee, and Mama orders [[brie]]. At the next table, a German couple greets the waiter. \"Hello, [[Herr]] Weber! Hello, [[Frau]] Weber!\" he answers in German. \"That's German for Mr. and Mrs.,\" Mama whispers. After lunch, Anna buys a red [[beret]] for twenty euros. On Sunday, they take a train to an old [[chateau]]. In the evening, they dress up [[a la]] old movie stars."},{"id":"c129","part":"p14","title":"Summer in Italy and Spain","level":"A2","words":["cruise","liner","gondola","canal","piazza","palace","souvenir","wine bar","chardonnay","pinot","pinot noir","compatriot"],"story":"This summer, Max and his parents go on a [[cruise]]. Their [[liner]] is as big as a small town. In Venice, they take a [[gondola]] along a narrow [[canal]]. Then they drink coffee in a [[piazza]] and see a pink [[palace]]. In Spain, Max buys a small guitar as a [[souvenir]] for Anna. In the evening, his parents sit in a [[wine bar]]. Mom orders a glass of [[chardonnay]], and Dad asks for a [[pinot]]. \"White or red?\" the waiter asks. \"Red, please, a [[pinot noir]],\" Dad says. A man at the next table hears them speak Ukrainian. He is a [[compatriot]] from Kyiv, and he lives near their street!"},{"id":"c130","part":"p14","title":"Rainy days in London","level":"A2","words":["trench coat","poncho","fleece","shawl","cape","scone","toffee","guinea"],"story":"Anna is taking a summer course in London. On the first day, it rains, and she gets very wet. Her teacher says, \"In London, you need a [[trench coat]].\" On Saturday, Anna buys a cheap [[poncho]] for rainy days. She also gets a soft [[fleece]] for cold mornings. She buys a long [[shawl]] for Mama and a wool [[cape]] for Grandma. She eats a [[scone]] with jam and buys [[toffee]] for Max. Later, she visits a small art museum. One old painting there once cost a hundred [[guineas|guinea]]. When Anna gets lost, a kind police officer helps her. She is wet, but happy."},{"id":"c131","part":"p14","title":"Max's Train Trip North","level":"B1","words":["echo","canton","fjord","Viking","geyser"],"story":"This summer, Max travels across Europe by train with one backpack. In Berlin, his hosts, Herr and Frau Weber, take him to a summer music fest. In the Alps, the nights are cold, so Max buys a warm cardigan. He sleeps in a wooden chalet below the castle of an old baron. When he shouts 'Hello!' from the hill, he hears a long [[echo]]. A local guide explains that every Swiss [[canton]] has its own flag. Everything is expensive, and his francs disappear very fast. In Norway, he pays in krone and takes a boat along a deep [[fjord]]. In a museum in Oslo, he sees an old [[Viking]] ship. His last stop is Iceland, where a [[geyser]] shoots hot water high into the air. Max sends Anna a photo: 'Next year, you are coming with me!'"},{"id":"c132","part":"p14","title":"Letters in Athens","level":"A2","words":["beta","alpha","gamma","kappa","mu","theta","phi","chi","sigma","omega","pi","labyrinth","delta"],"story":"Anna is in Athens with Max, but she can't read Greek signs. Max opens the [[beta]] of a new app for learning letters. The first letter is [[alpha]], and the third is [[gamma]]. Anna finds [[kappa]] and [[mu]] on a bus sign. On a café menu, she sees [[theta]] and [[phi]]. [[Chi|chi]] looks like an X, and [[sigma]] looks a bit like E. \"And [[omega]] is the last one!\" Max says. \"I know [[pi]] from math class,\" Anna laughs. Later, they get lost in a garden [[labyrinth]]. Anna reads the Greek exit sign and finds the way out! On the plane home, they see a green river [[delta]] below."},{"id":"c133","part":"p14","title":"Two Weeks in Tokyo","level":"A2","words":["sushi","ramen","kimono","geisha","sakura","etiquette"],"story":"Max spent two weeks with his friend Kenji in Tokyo. On the first night, they ate [[sushi]] near the station. The next day, they had hot [[ramen]] for lunch. Max bought three manga books for his little sister. In the park, he saw a woman in a beautiful [[kimono]]. Later, a [[geisha]] walked slowly under the pink [[sakura]] trees. At dinner, Max did not know the table [[etiquette]]. Kenji's senpai showed him how to hold chopsticks. On the last weekend, a typhoon hit the city. They stayed inside, played games and laughed all day."},{"id":"c134","part":"p14","title":"Backpacking in Asia","level":"B1","words":["kimchi","oppa","bao","dong","durian","papaya","malaria"],"story":"Anna's friend Lisa went backpacking in Asia last summer and slept in cheap hostels. In Seoul, she ate [[kimchi]] with two girls who loved K-pop. When their favorite singer walked on stage, they screamed, \"[[Oppa|oppa]]!\" In China, she had pork [[bao]] for breakfast and a sweet mandarin after it. The whole meal cost only twenty yuan. In Vietnam, she rented a moped and paid for it in [[dong]]. In Thailand, a market woman sold her fruit for a hundred baht. Lisa tried [[durian]], but the smell was too strong for her. She liked the [[papaya]] much more. Before her trip, a doctor gave her pills against [[malaria]], just in case. Lisa came home tired, happy, and full of stories."},{"id":"c135","part":"p14","title":"A Wedding in India","level":"B1","words":["sari","dhoti","turban","Sikh","raja","maharaja","sahib","cobra","puja","mystic","Sanskrit","prasad"],"story":"Anna's college friend Priya invited her to a wedding in India. All the women wore bright [[saris|sari]], and Anna wore a borrowed one too. Priya's grandfather wore a white [[dhoti]], and her uncle wore a red [[turban]]. The uncle is a [[Sikh]], and he loves telling old stories. He told Anna about a [[raja]] who ruled a small kingdom near a river. His neighbor was a [[maharaja]], a much greater king with a far bigger palace. In the story, a foreign visitor made the servants call him [[sahib]]. After lunch, a snake charmer showed the guests a [[cobra]] in a basket. In the evening, the family went to the temple for a [[puja]]. An old [[mystic]] read prayers in [[Sanskrit]] with his eyes closed. At the end, he gave everyone sweet [[prasad]]. Anna said it was the most beautiful day of her year."},{"id":"c136","part":"p14","title":"Istanbul, Dubai and Cairo","level":"B1","words":["bazaar","sheikh","emirate","emir","oasis","mirage","scorpion","sphinx"],"story":"Max's parents took a long trip around the Middle East this spring. In Istanbul, they went shopping in an old [[bazaar]] and bought a blue amulet for Max. In Dubai, they visited a palace where a [[sheikh]] once welcomed guests. The guide said that Dubai is the biggest city of its [[emirate]]. In a nearby country, the ruler has a different title: he is the [[emir]]. Then they rode camels across the desert to a green [[oasis]]. On the way, Max's dad saw a lake, but it was only a [[mirage]]. In the morning, a [[scorpion]] was sleeping in his shoe! In Cairo, they heard the morning prayers at an old mosque. They saw the Great [[Sphinx|sphinx]] and took a boat trip on the Nile. Back home, Max's dad laughed and said he now checks his shoes every morning."},{"id":"c137","part":"p14","title":"A Safari in Kenya","level":"B1","words":["safari","equator","tropics","continent","hyena","gazelle","savanna","shea"],"story":"Anna's aunt Olena always wanted to see wild animals. Her travel agent found her a cheap [[safari]] in Kenya. Kenya lies right on the [[equator]], so it was hot every day. Olena had never been to the [[tropics]] before. It was her first time on another [[continent]], too. On the first night, she heard a [[hyena]] laughing in the dark. In the morning, a young [[gazelle]] ran past her jeep. The wide [[savanna]] looked golden in the sun. At a village market, she paid fifty shillings for a jar of [[shea]] butter. Then she flew to South Africa and changed her money into rand. She came home with a suntan and a thousand photos."},{"id":"c138","part":"p14","title":"Max in Latin America","level":"B1","words":["cactus","llama","condor","coca","machete","piranha"],"story":"Max traveled to Mexico, where his new friend Diego met him at the bus station. \"Welcome, amigo!\" Diego said, and he paid for the taxi with two hundred pesos. In the evening, Diego's uncles drank tequila at a small cafe. Max ordered a margarita without alcohol and watched the sun set behind a tall [[cactus]]. A week later, the two friends flew to Peru. In the mountains, a [[llama]] carried their heavy bags. Their guide said a puma sometimes walks near this trail. High above them, a huge [[condor]] flew in slow circles. They passed small farms where [[coca]] grows on green hills. In the Amazon jungle, the guide cut a path with a [[machete]]. A caiman watched them quietly from the river bank. The guide said the river was full of [[piranhas|piranha]], so Max stayed in the boat."},{"id":"c139","part":"p14","title":"Summer Down Under","level":"B1","words":["kangaroo","koala","dingo","boomerang","crab","bikini","topless","tiki"],"story":"Anna's cousin Dan got a summer job at a beach resort in Australia. On his first day off, he saw a [[kangaroo]] jumping across the road. In a tall tree, a sleepy [[koala]] did not even open its eyes. Near the forest, a wild [[dingo]] watched him and then ran away. A local boy taught Dan how to throw a [[boomerang]]. For dinner, they ate fresh [[crab]] on the beach. Dan slept in a small bungalow by the sea. One night, a strong cyclone hit the coast, but his little house stayed safe. On a small island nearby, tourists in bright [[bikinis|bikini]] read a sign: \"No [[topless]] sunbathing.\" A wooden [[tiki]] stood at the door of the beach bar. Far away, red lava glowed at the top of an old volcano. In the evening, Dan played the ukulele for his new friends by the fire."},{"id":"c140","part":"p14","title":"A Week in New York","level":"A2","words":["Chinatown","bagel","cream cheese","steak","lobster"],"story":"Anna and Max spent a week in New York in October. Their hotel was downtown, near a wide boulevard. A huge billboard over the street showed a smiling cat. On the first evening, they ate dumplings in [[Chinatown]]. On Sunday morning, they went to brunch at a small cafe. Anna ate a warm [[bagel]] with [[cream cheese]]. Max had a big plate of French toast. On the way back, Anna found a dime on the street. \"It's lucky money!\" she said and laughed. On their last night, they had dinner with Max's cousin Ben. Max ordered a [[steak]], and Anna tried [[lobster]] for the first time. Then they watched the city lights from Ben's penthouse."},{"id":"c141","part":"p15","title":"Dad's Small Bakery","level":"B1","words":["businessman","businesswoman","business partner","business plan","cash flow","profit","pricing","vendor","dealer","retailer","retail","sales manager","cooperative","barter","distributor"],"story":"Last year, Anna's dad decided to become a [[businessman]]. Anna's mom, a [[businesswoman]] with her own flower shop, gave him lots of advice. He opened a small bakery with his old friend Taras, who became his [[business partner]]. First, they wrote a [[business plan]], and Anna helped them check the [[cash flow]] every week. After six months, the bakery made its first small [[profit]]. They kept their [[pricing]] simple: every pie cost the same. They chose a local [[vendor]] for flour and bought a delivery van from a [[dealer]]. Soon a big [[retailer]] wanted to sell their bread in its stores. Taras had worked in [[retail]] before, so he knew what to say. They hired a [[sales manager]] named Iryna and joined a farmers' [[cooperative]] for fresh milk. Sometimes they even used [[barter]] and paid the farmers with fresh bread. Now a regional [[distributor]] takes their pies to five towns."},{"id":"c142","part":"p15","title":"Max's Startup","level":"B1","words":["startup","founder","concept","business model","use case","investor","game changer","win-win","venture","capital","know-how","patent","innovator","joint venture"],"story":"Max and two friends started their own [[startup]] last spring. As the [[founder]], Max had to explain the idea to everyone. The [[concept]] was simple: an app that plans cheap, healthy meals for students. Their [[business model]] was a small monthly payment. Max showed a simple [[use case]]: a tired student opens the app and finds dinner. An [[investor]] named Mrs. Bondar listened carefully. She said the app could be a [[game changer]] for busy students. She offered them a [[win-win]] deal and asked to join their [[venture]]. She put in the [[capital]], and the team brought their [[know-how]]. Soon they got a [[patent]] for their smart shopping list. A newspaper called Max a young [[innovator]], and his mom put it on the fridge. Now a food delivery company wants to start a [[joint venture]] with them in Poland."},{"id":"c143","part":"p15","title":"Anna's Marketing Seminar","level":"B1","words":["marketing","seminar","case study","branding","art director","logo","slogan","targeting","mass market","respondent","benchmark","promotion","landing page","email marketing","workshop","symposium"],"story":"Anna is studying [[marketing]], and on Friday she went to a [[seminar]] at her university. The teacher gave the class a [[case study]] about a small juice company with weak [[branding]]. A real [[art director]] helped Anna's team create a new [[logo]] and a [[slogan]]. Then they talked about [[targeting]] and decided to sell the juice to the [[mass market]]. Most [[respondents|respondent]] in a survey liked the green bottles. They compared their sales numbers with a [[benchmark]] from a bigger company. Anna suggested a summer [[promotion]]: buy two bottles, get one free. They also designed a simple [[landing page]] and planned some [[email marketing]] for old customers. Next week, Anna has a hands-on [[workshop]] where students make real ads together. In May, professors from many countries will give long talks at a big [[symposium]]. The teacher liked Anna's project so much that she can present it there!"},{"id":"c144","part":"p15","title":"A tech expo","level":"B1","words":["expo","keynote","product manager","sponsor","banner","promoter","flyer","bestseller","press release","high-tech","poster","billboard","high tech"],"story":"Last weekend, Anna helped her friend at a big tech [[expo]] in Kyiv. The [[keynote]] was given by a famous businesswoman who started as a [[product manager]]. Every [[sponsor]] hung a bright [[banner]] above its stand. At the door, a young [[promoter]] handed Anna a [[flyer]] about a new book. The book, about smart robots, was already a [[bestseller]]. At noon, the team sent a [[press release]] to all the news sites. In her talk, the businesswoman said she had worked in [[high-tech]] for twenty years. After the talk, Anna got a free [[poster]] of a smiling robot for her room. On the way home, she saw the same robot on a huge [[billboard]] by the road. That evening, Anna told Max she wanted a job in [[high tech]] one day."},{"id":"c145","part":"p15","title":"A Day at the Port","level":"B1","words":["port","dock","tanker","ballast","barrel","cargo","conveyor","export","import","exporter","importer","tariff","quota","industrialist"],"story":"On Saturday, Max visited his uncle Petro at the [[port]] of Odesa. A big ship was waiting in the [[dock]] for repairs. Next to it, an empty oil [[tanker]] carried only seawater as [[ballast]]. \"That ship brings oil, and a [[barrel]] costs more every month,\" his uncle said. In the warehouse, boxes of [[cargo]] moved slowly along a [[conveyor]]. \"Grain is our main [[export]], and this coffee is an [[import]] from South America,\" he explained. \"So I am an [[exporter]] and an [[importer]] at the same time.\" Max asked why the coffee was so expensive. \"New [[tariffs|tariff]] on coffee, and each company has a yearly [[quota]] too,\" Uncle Petro sighed. Then a rich [[industrialist]] in a gray suit arrived at the office. He wanted to start a joint venture with Max's uncle. That evening, Max told Anna he might study business after all."},{"id":"c146","part":"p15","title":"Uncle Oleh, the trader","level":"B1","words":["trader","trading","broker","brokerage","index","dividend","bitcoin","smart money","futures","derivative","hedge fund","broker-dealer","asset management"],"story":"Anna's uncle Oleh works as a [[trader]] at a big bank in Kyiv. At Sunday lunch, Anna asked him what [[trading]] really is. \"I buy and sell shares for people, a bit like a [[broker]],\" he said. \"You can open your own account at a [[brokerage]] with very little money.\" He showed her the stock market [[index]] on his phone. \"This company pays me a [[dividend]] every quarter,\" he smiled. Then he admitted that he also bought some [[bitcoin]] last year. \"Most people just try to follow the [[smart money]],\" he added. He also explained oil [[futures]] and a strange [[derivative]] that nobody at the table understood. His old friend now runs a [[hedge fund]] abroad. \"He started at a [[broker-dealer]], a firm that trades for clients and for itself,\" Oleh said. Anna laughed and said she would study [[asset management]], starting with her pocket money."},{"id":"c147","part":"p15","title":"Buying a New Flat","level":"B1","words":["developer","consortium","banking","grace period","escrow","creditor","reserve","auditor","audit"],"story":"Anna's parents finally decided to buy a new flat. A local [[developer]] is building the house, and a [[consortium]] of banks is paying for it. It will be a modern condominium with a small park and a playground. Anna's mother, who works in [[banking]], quickly found them a good loan. The loan even has a six-month [[grace period]] before the first payment. Their money will stay in [[escrow]] until the flat is ready. The bank, as their [[creditor]], checked how much money they keep in [[reserve]]. The city also gave them a small rebate for choosing an energy-saving home. Anna's father still worried, so he called his friend, an [[auditor]]. She said the building company had a clean [[audit]] last year. That night, the whole family looked at the plans and chose Anna's future room."},{"id":"c148","part":"p15","title":"The economy on TV","level":"B1","words":["economist","boom","collapse","deficit","trillion","default","insider","risk management","tax-free","million"],"story":"Anna and Max were watching the evening news at Max's apartment. An [[economist]] in a blue jacket talked about a [[boom]] in online shopping. \"But some small shops are close to [[collapse]],\" she warned. Then she explained what a budget [[deficit]] is, using a simple chart. \"Some countries owe more than a [[trillion]] dollars,\" she said. \"When a country cannot pay its debts, we call it [[default]],\" the economist continued. Next, a bank [[insider]] told reporters how criminals tried to hide their money. Thanks to good [[risk management]], the bank stopped them in time. Anna yawned and changed the channel to an ad for [[tax-free]] shopping at the airport. \"I can't even imagine a [[million]] dollars,\" Max joked. \"Airport shopping is the only economy I understand.\""},{"id":"c149","part":"p15","title":"A party for the rich","level":"B1","words":["cocktail party","burlesque","self-made","millionaire","magnate","conglomerate","business interest","box office","caviar","banquet","gala","endowment"],"story":"Max's rich cousin Denys invited him to a [[cocktail party]] in a fancy hotel. The evening started with a funny old-style [[burlesque]] show with songs and jokes. Denys introduced Max to a [[self-made]] businessman from a small village. The man became a [[millionaire]] before he turned thirty. Next to him stood an oil [[magnate]] who owned a huge [[conglomerate]]. \"I have [[business interests|business interest]] in five countries,\" he told Max proudly. A group of actors were discussing their new movie. \"It did great at the [[box office]],\" one actress said, eating [[caviar]] on tiny crackers. \"Tomorrow's [[banquet]] is different, with a long dinner and speeches,\" she added. \"And next month there's a charity [[gala]], the most elegant night of the year.\" Later, a quiet old man gave a big [[endowment]] to the university where Max studies. Max decided that was the most impressive thing he saw all night."},{"id":"c150","part":"p15","title":"Consultants at the Office","level":"B1","words":["consultant","consulting","business center","project management","recruiting","memorandum","directorate","pharma","shredder","auction","middle manager"],"story":"On Monday, a [[consultant]] named Laura arrived at Max's company. She works in [[consulting]] and visits a new company every month. She invited everyone to a hall in the [[business center]] for a workshop. First, she talked about [[project management]] and how to plan tasks better. Then she discussed [[recruiting]] and how to find talented young people. After lunch, she wrote a long [[memorandum]] for the company's [[directorate]]. It also gave advice about working with clients in [[pharma]]. Max helped her put boxes of old papers into the [[shredder]]. The company even sold its old furniture at an [[auction]]. Every [[middle manager]] in the office was worried about their job. But on Friday, Laura said the team was doing great, and everyone finally relaxed."},{"id":"f01","part":"p15","title":"Grandpa's coin collection","level":"A2","words":["euro","sterling","franc","krone","yuan","baht","lira","dinar","shilling","rand","peso","ruble"],"story":"On Sunday, Grandpa showed Anna and Taras his old box of money. First, he took out a shiny [[euro]] from a trip to Italy. \"This is a British pound, also called [[sterling]],\" he said. Next came an old French [[franc]] and a Danish [[krone]]. Taras found a red Chinese [[yuan]] note under the coins. Anna liked a Thai [[baht]] coin with a temple on it. Grandpa also had a Turkish [[lira]] and a [[dinar]] from Jordan. \"A Kenyan [[shilling]] and a South African [[rand]],\" Taras read slowly. At the bottom lay a Mexican [[peso]] and an old [[ruble]]. \"Every coin has a story from my travels,\" Grandpa smiled. That evening, Anna and Taras started their own collection."},{"id":"c151","part":"p16","title":"A Meeting at City Hall","level":"B1","words":["prefect","mayor","alderman","zoning","urban design","smart city","bureaucrat","bulldozer","community center","kiosk","barbershop","depot","squatter"],"story":"On Tuesday evening, Anna and Max went to a meeting at city hall about their street. On the wall hung a painting of an old [[prefect]] who ruled for an emperor. The [[mayor]] and a local [[alderman]] sat under it and opened the meeting. First, they talked about new [[zoning]] rules and modern [[urban design]]. \"We want Kyiv to become a [[smart city]] with apps and sensors,\" she said. A tired [[bureaucrat]] showed everyone a pile of papers and maps. Then the neighbors got angry. \"A [[bulldozer]] will destroy our [[community center]]!\" one woman shouted. Others worried about the old [[kiosk]], the [[barbershop]] and the bus [[depot]]. \"Some [[squatters|squatter]] live there now, and they need help,\" an old man added. Finally, the city leaders promised to save the places people loved, and everyone clapped."},{"id":"c152","part":"p16","title":"Anna Volunteers","level":"B1","words":["volunteer","charity","fundraiser","fundraising","veteran","advocacy","pauper","handmade","heroism","patriotism"],"story":"This autumn, Anna became a [[volunteer]] at a small [[charity]] in Kyiv. Her boss, Iryna, is a professional [[fundraiser]] with endless energy. Together they do [[fundraising]] for war [[veterans|veteran]] and their families. They also collect money for a little boy with lymphoma. The charity does [[advocacy]] for old people who live like [[paupers|pauper]] in cold houses. On Saturday, Anna sold forty [[handmade]] cards at the market. After that, she laid flowers at the war memorial in the park. She thought about the soldiers' [[heroism]] and felt quiet [[patriotism]] in her heart. Then Iryna called with good news: the boy's family now had enough money for treatment."},{"id":"c153","part":"p16","title":"New neighbors","level":"B1","words":["immigrant","green card","consulate","consul","racism","racist","ghetto","middle class","baby boom","baby boomer","boomer","nationalist","nationalism","millennial","migrant"],"story":"A family of [[immigrants|immigrant]] moved into Anna's building last week. Their son lives in America and just got his [[green card]]. Last month, their daughter Lina visited the [[consulate]], where the [[consul]] helped her with papers. Lina told Anna about [[racism]] at her old school and a [[racist]] neighbor there. Before Kyiv, the family lived in a poor [[ghetto]] in a big, noisy city. Now her parents work hard and hope to join the [[middle class]] here. Anna's grandpa was born during the [[baby boom]], so he is a real [[baby boomer]]. Max smiled and said young people just say \"[[boomer]]\" for short. Grandpa calls himself a [[nationalist]], so Lina asked him what that means. They had a long, friendly argument about [[nationalism]], while Lina's brother, a [[millennial]], listened. In the end, Grandpa smiled and said, \"Every [[migrant]] is welcome at my table.\""},{"id":"c154","part":"p16","title":"Election Night Drama","level":"B1","words":["broadcaster","president","vice president","candidate","democrat","liberal","social democrat","electorate","mandate","primaries","caucus","referendum","Tory","loyalist","charisma"],"story":"On Sunday night, Anna and Max watched the last episode of their favorite political drama. In the show, a national [[broadcaster]] covers election night in an imaginary country. The old [[president]] and his [[vice president]] wait nervously in their office. Each [[candidate]] gives a speech: a [[democrat]], a [[liberal]] and a [[social democrat]]. They all say they understand the [[electorate]] and want a strong [[mandate]]. Earlier in the season, Max got confused about the [[primaries]] and the [[caucus]]. Anna explained them, and also the [[referendum]] from episode three. A funny British guest, a [[Tory]], keeps comparing everything to London. Outside, a crowd of [[loyalists|loyalist]] waves flags for the old leader. In the end, a young woman with lots of [[charisma]] wins. Max clapped and asked, \"Can we watch the next season tomorrow?\""},{"id":"c155","part":"p16","title":"A day in parliament","level":"B1","words":["parliament","agenda","briefing","minister","premier","senate","senator","congress","congressman","congresswoman","lobbyist","lobby","compromise","consensus","status quo","shutdown","impeachment","de facto"],"story":"On Thursday, Anna's class visited [[parliament]], and a guide explained each party's political [[agenda]]. At a press [[briefing]], a young [[minister]] talked about schools, and the [[premier]] discussed the budget. Mr. Koval explained that some countries have a [[senate]], where each [[senator]] votes on laws. \"In America, the Senate is one part of [[Congress|congress]],\" he added. \"The other part, the House, has hundreds of [[congressmen|congressman]] and [[congresswomen|congresswoman]].\" In the hall, a [[lobbyist]] from the energy [[lobby]] waited with a thick folder. The members argued for hours but finally reached a [[compromise]]. The guide said full [[consensus]] is rare, because many people just want the [[status quo]]. Now they had a budget, so there would be no [[shutdown]] this year. Anna asked about [[impeachment]], and Mr. Koval explained it with a funny example. On the bus home, Max asked so many questions that he became the [[de facto]] guide."},{"id":"c156","part":"p16","title":"A Summit in Geneva","level":"B1","words":["summit","secretariat","diplomat","delegate","bloc","alliance","pact","embargo","veto"],"story":"Last week, Anna's aunt Olena worked as an interpreter at a [[summit]] in Geneva. On the first morning, she picked up her badge at the [[secretariat]] on the second floor. The hall was full of [[diplomats|diplomat]] and nervous [[delegates|delegate]] from many countries. Each [[bloc]] wanted to build a stronger [[alliance]] with its neighbors. On the second day, two small countries signed a peace [[pact]]. They also talked about ending an [[embargo]] on fruit and grain. One leader threatened to use his [[veto]], but in the end he agreed. An emir in white robes gave a short, warm speech. Then the elderly sovereign of a tiny island kingdom spoke about the ocean. An American congressman and a congresswoman from the same state spoke too. Olena translated every word without a single mistake. \"Next month, a medical congress will feel easy,\" she told Anna that night."},{"id":"c157","part":"p16","title":"Students protest","level":"B1","words":["protest","activist","activism","ideal","idealism","utopia","trade union","strike","boycott","anarchist","cynic","hypocrite","nonsense"],"story":"On Saturday, Anna and Max joined a student [[protest]] near the university. The city wanted to close the student library and build a parking lot. A young [[activist]], Sofia, said her [[activism]] began in a library like this one. \"We have one [[ideal]]: free books for everyone,\" she said. Max liked her [[idealism]], but he did not believe in a perfect [[utopia]]. Then workers from a local [[trade union]] arrived with big signs. They promised a one-day [[strike]] and called for a [[boycott]] of the parking company. A man in a black hat said he was an [[anarchist]] and shouted at the sky. Max's friend Oleh, a real [[cynic]], called all the politicians [[hypocrites|hypocrite]]. He said the whole march was [[nonsense]]. Two weeks later, the city kept the library open, and even Oleh brought cake."},{"id":"c158","part":"p16","title":"A debate about rights","level":"B1","words":["feminism","feminist","sexism","homophobia","pro-choice","pro-life","antisemitism","apartheid","extremist","skinhead","supremacist","euthanasia"],"story":"On Friday, Anna's class held a big debate about human rights. First, Anna talked about the history of [[feminism]]. She said her grandmother was the first [[feminist]] she ever knew. Max gave examples of [[sexism]] in sports and in job ads. Then Iryna spoke about [[homophobia]] in schools. She said every gay student should feel as safe as anyone else. Next, two students shared [[pro-choice]] and [[pro-life]] views and listened to each other politely. The history part was hard: they learned about [[antisemitism]] and [[apartheid]]. They also discussed how an [[extremist]] spreads hate online. In a short film, a young [[skinhead]] left a group of white [[supremacists|supremacist]] forever. The last topic was [[euthanasia]], and nobody agreed at all. Still, their teacher smiled: \"You argued, but you respected each other.\""},{"id":"c159","part":"p16","title":"Left and right","level":"B1","words":["communism","capitalism","socialism","Marxism","proletariat","communist","socialist","capitalist","anti-communist","liberalism"],"story":"In politics class, Professor Lysenko drew two big circles on the board. One said [[communism]], and the other said [[capitalism]]. \"Between them, you find [[socialism]] and many other ideas,\" he said. He explained that [[Marxism]] was a theory from the nineteenth century. In that theory, the [[proletariat]] were the workers in the factories. \"A [[communist]] wants the state to own almost everything,\" he said. \"A [[socialist]] wants fair taxes and free schools. A [[capitalist]] wants free markets and private business.\" Max told the class about his great-grandfather, a strong [[anti-communist]]. \"But his neighbor called everyone comrade, even the mailman,\" Max laughed. At the end, the professor wrote one more word: [[liberalism]]. \"Next week, we argue about freedom,\" he said, and the class groaned happily."},{"id":"c160","part":"p16","title":"Anna's internship at a newspaper","level":"B1","words":["newsroom","journalist","columnist","editorial","correspondent","exclusive","scandal","tabloid","publicity","PR","publisher","digest","rewrite","narrative","media","reporter","mass media"],"story":"In July, Anna started a month-long internship in a busy [[newsroom]]. An older [[journalist]] named Petro showed her how to check every fact. Next to him sat a [[columnist]] who was writing the Sunday [[editorial]]. At noon, a [[correspondent]] abroad called with an [[exclusive]]: a [[scandal]] at a famous football club. A [[tabloid]] already had rumors about it. \"They want [[publicity]], not facts,\" Petro said. Meanwhile, the club's [[PR]] people kept calling to stop the story. The [[publisher]] read the morning [[digest]] and asked for a quick [[rewrite]]. He wanted the true story, not the old [[narrative]] about the club. By evening, the [[media]] waited outside the club, and a TV [[reporter]] went live. Petro let Anna write the headline. The next morning, the [[mass media]] everywhere repeated it."},{"id":"c161","part":"p16","title":"Anna's cousin in the army","level":"B1","words":["cadet","officer","recruit","lieutenant","sergeant","battalion","convoy","checkpoint","bunker","camouflage","drone","tank","combatant","adjutant","commandant","commodore","admiral","patriot","parade"],"story":"Anna's cousin Taras was a [[cadet]] only four years ago. Now he is an [[officer]], and he trains every new [[recruit]]. On Sunday, he visited Anna and told stories over tea. His [[lieutenant]] is strict but fair, and his [[sergeant]] tells terrible jokes. Last month, his [[battalion]] moved a [[convoy]] of trucks through a [[checkpoint]]. They slept in a cold [[bunker]] and wore [[camouflage]] in the forest. A small [[drone]] watched them from above, and a [[tank]] moved slowly behind. In the exercise, half of the soldiers played enemy [[combatants|combatant]]. Taras was the colonel's [[adjutant]], so he carried orders to the base [[commandant]] on foot. Grandpa laughed and said he once served under a navy [[commodore]], one step below an [[admiral]]. Asked why he joined, Taras said, \"I'm a [[patriot]], and I want my family safe.\" Most of all, they all dream of marching in a big peace [[parade]] together."},{"id":"c162","part":"p17","title":"Who Stole Max's Bike?","level":"B1","words":["cop","detective","silhouette","shoplifting","vandalism","alibi","pretext","dossier","polygraph","vandal","hooligan","policeman","constable","sheriff"],"story":"One morning, Max's bike was gone from the street outside his building. He called the [[cops|cop]], and a young [[detective]] named Koval came an hour later. On the street camera, they saw the [[silhouette]] of a tall man at night. Koval knew him: a local guy with a history of [[shoplifting]] and [[vandalism]]. He had an [[alibi]]: he said he was at his aunt's house all night. The next day, he came back on the [[pretext]] of walking his dog. Koval checked his [[dossier]] and asked for a [[polygraph]] test. Before the test even started, the young [[vandal]] confessed. He and an old soccer [[hooligan]] friend took the bike as a stupid joke. That evening, a friendly [[policeman]] brought the bike back to Max. Max's grandpa smiled: \"In old British novels, he would be a [[constable]].\" \"And in cowboy movies, he would be the [[sheriff]],\" Max laughed."},{"id":"c163","part":"p17","title":"A hacker on trial","level":"B1","words":["hacker","hacking","scam","warez","peer-to-peer","copyright","barrister","pro bono","precedent","affidavit","bailiff","tribunal","verdict","disclaimer"],"story":"Anna's law class visited a real courtroom on Tuesday. A young [[hacker]] named Denys sat quietly next to his lawyer. He was on trial for [[hacking]] into a game company and running an email [[scam]]. He also sold [[warez]] on a [[peer-to-peer]] network, against [[copyright]] law. His [[barrister]], an older woman, worked [[pro bono]] because Denys had no money. She talked about an old [[precedent]] and showed an [[affidavit]] from his teacher. Then the [[bailiff]] asked everyone to stand. The [[tribunal]] read its [[verdict]]: guilty, but with a second chance. Now Denys must help a bank find weak spots in its apps. He even has to read every [[disclaimer]] before he clicks \"I agree.\""},{"id":"c164","part":"p17","title":"Gangs and Drugs","level":"B1","words":["mafia","gangster","yakuza","vendetta","trafficking","cartel","syndicate","raid","bong","pistol","revolver","shotgun","caliber"],"story":"On Friday night, Max watched an old film about the [[mafia]] with his dad. In it, an old [[gangster]] flies to Tokyo to meet the [[yakuza]]. The two groups start a long [[vendetta]] over drug [[trafficking]]. Soon a rival drug [[cartel]] wants the same routes. Behind them all is a huge crime [[syndicate]]. In the end, a police [[raid]] stops everything in one night. In the basement, the police find a [[bong]], a [[pistol]], an old [[revolver]], and a [[shotgun]]. An expert checks the [[caliber]] of every bullet. Max's dad fell asleep before the end, so Max had to tell him everything."},{"id":"c165","part":"p17","title":"A True-Crime Podcast","level":"B1","words":["maniac","psychopath","sociopath","sadist","abuser","abuse","stalking","kidnapping","chloroform","pedophile","incest","coroner","morgue","cannibalism"],"story":"Anna listens to a true-crime podcast on her way to class. This week, the host talks about a [[maniac]] from an old case. One doctor calls him a [[psychopath]], but another says he was more of a [[sociopath]]. Both agree that he was a [[sadist]] who enjoyed other people's pain. He was also a cruel [[abuser]], and his family lived with years of [[abuse]]. Later, he began [[stalking]] young women in his town. The police finally stopped him after a failed [[kidnapping]] with [[chloroform]]. In the second part, an expert explains how to protect children from a [[pedophile]] online. She also explains why [[incest]] and other family crimes often stay hidden. Then a [[coroner]] describes her work in the city [[morgue]]. She laughs and says her hobby is [[cannibalism]] in spiders. Anna takes off her headphones and decides to listen to music tonight."},{"id":"c166","part":"p17","title":"A thriller about terror","level":"B1","words":["terrorism","terrorist","jihadist","insurgent","separatist","sabotage","detonator","arsenal","aggressor","escort","sniper"],"story":"Anna is reading a thriller about the fight against [[terrorism]] in an imaginary country. In the book, a [[terrorist]] group plans an attack on a big port. Its leader is a [[jihadist]], and his men are [[insurgents|insurgent]] from the mountains. They join forces with a [[separatist]] army from the north. Together, they plan [[sabotage]] at the main power station. But the police find a [[detonator]] in an old car. Then they discover a whole [[arsenal]] of weapons on a farm. The commandant of the base sends soldiers and a young medic. A navy ship uses sonar to find the [[aggressors|aggressor]]' small boat. The president arrives at the port with a special [[escort]]. A police [[sniper]] watches the crowd from a roof. The attack never happens, and Anna finally falls asleep at 2 a.m."},{"id":"c167","part":"p18","title":"Max Builds a Computer","level":"B1","words":["manual","component","processor","chip","slot","input","output","prototype","transistor","byte"],"story":"Max decided to build his own computer instead of buying one. He spread all the new parts over the kitchen table. First, he read the [[manual]] carefully, page by page. He checked every [[component]] and placed the [[processor]], the main [[chip]], very gently. He pushed extra memory into each [[slot]] for faster games. Then he tested the keyboard [[input]] and the screen [[output]] with a small program. A tiny error appeared, but he fixed it in five minutes. That evening, his friend Ira brought an old [[prototype]] from her grandfather's garage. Its [[transistors|transistor]] were huge, and it could hold only one [[byte]] at a time. Max laughed: his new computer was a million times faster."},{"id":"c168","part":"p18","title":"Max Learns Coding","level":"B1","words":["programmer","coding","software engineer","test case","tester","log","open source","bot","prompt","contributor","plug-in","API","add-on","mod"],"story":"At Max's company, a [[programmer]] named Lena offered to teach him [[coding]]. Her official title is [[software engineer]], but she says it is the same job. On his first day, Max wrote a simple [[test case]] for the login page. A [[tester]] ran it and then read the [[log]] with him. Next, the team started a small [[open source]] project: a friendly help [[bot]]. The bot answers any [[prompt]] about the city's buses. Soon a [[contributor]] from Lviv added a [[plug-in]] for the weather. It uses a free weather [[API]], so the bot knows when it rains. A week later, a student made a small [[add-on]] with train times too. Max asked the bot, \"Do I need an umbrella?\" It said yes. That night, Max felt brave and made his first [[mod]] for his favorite game. Next week, the bot goes to real users, and Max is a little nervous."},{"id":"c169","part":"p18","title":"Building a Podcast Website","level":"B1","words":["domain","hosting","web design","redesign","back end","interface","pixel","rendering","post-processing","real-time"],"story":"Anna wanted a website for her podcast, so she called Max for help. First, Max bought a [[domain]] with the podcast's name. Then he paid for [[hosting]] on a fast web server. \"I love [[web design]],\" he said, \"and your old logo needs a [[redesign]] too.\" He spent two evenings on the [[back end]], and Anna tested the simple [[interface]]. Max checked every [[pixel]] of the new logo in his web browser. \"Why is the video page so slow?\" Anna asked. Max explained that [[rendering]] big videos takes time on a small laptop. He also showed her how good [[post-processing]] makes her photos bright and clean. Finally, he added a [[real-time]] chat for her listeners. On Friday, the first fan wrote, \"Great new site!\""},{"id":"c170","part":"p18","title":"A visit to a data center","level":"B1","words":["data center","server","web server","mainframe","cache","firewall","batch","Internet Protocol","IP","buffer","computing","transmitter","ping","lag"],"story":"On Monday, Max's team visited a big [[data center]] outside the city. Oleh, a friendly admin, showed them long rows of machines, and every [[server]] had blinking lights. \"That one is a [[web server]]; it sends websites to your phone,\" Oleh said. In the corner stood an old [[mainframe]] that still worked. \"We keep popular pages in the [[cache]], so they open fast,\" he explained. \"And our [[firewall]] stops strange connections every minute.\" He showed how each [[batch]] of data travels with the [[Internet Protocol]], or [[IP]] for short. \"Data waits in a [[buffer]] for a moment before it leaves,\" he added. \"That's why cloud [[computing]] is so cheap for small companies.\" On the roof, Max saw a tall radio [[transmitter]]. Back at the office, he played an online game, and his [[ping]] was lower than ever. There was no [[lag]] at all!"},{"id":"c171","part":"p18","title":"Anna Learns Data Science","level":"B1","words":["data science","algorithm","cluster","big data","dataset","parameter","coefficient","vector","gradient","parallel","quadrant"],"story":"This fall, Anna started an online [[data science]] course. In the first lesson, she learned how an [[algorithm]] suggests songs to listeners. It finds each [[cluster]] of people with similar taste. \"This is [[big data]],\" the teacher said, \"millions of songs and listeners.\" For homework, Anna got a small [[dataset]] about coffee shops in Kyiv. She changed one [[parameter]] and watched the results change. In the formula 3x, the [[coefficient]] was three, so the line went up fast. Then she drew a [[vector]] as an arrow on the graph. She colored the background with a soft blue [[gradient]]. Anna noticed a funny [[parallel]] between coffee orders and music taste. When she got bored, she drew a little spiral in the margin. The best café sat in the upper right [[quadrant]], with cheap coffee and great music."},{"id":"c172","part":"p18","title":"A physics lesson","level":"B1","words":["stasis","atom","electron","proton","neutron","photon","quark","neutrino","vacuum","plasma","impulse","resonance","magnet"],"story":"After summer, Taras felt his brain was in [[stasis]], but his physics teacher woke him up. \"Everything around you is made of [[atoms|atom]],\" she said. She drew a tiny [[electron]] flying around a [[proton]] and a [[neutron]]. \"Light is made of [[photons|photon]], and a [[quark]] is even smaller than a proton,\" she added. \"A [[neutrino]] is even stranger, because it can fly through the whole Earth.\" Then she put a ringing phone in a glass jar and pumped out the air. In the [[vacuum]], nobody could hear the phone. \"Lightning is a kind of [[plasma]],\" she said, pointing at the storm outside. She explained that each nerve sends an electric [[impulse]] to the brain. Then she sang one high note, and a glass on her desk began to shake. \"That's [[resonance]],\" she laughed. At the end, she gave everyone a [[magnet]], and Taras couldn't wait for more."},{"id":"c173","part":"p18","title":"The Lemon Battery Project","level":"B1","words":["watt","volt","voltage","ohm","henry","SI","electrode","ion","nickel","zinc","cobalt","reactor"],"story":"On Saturday, Max helped Taras with his science project about electricity. First, they read the label on a lamp: sixty [[watts|watt]]. A small battery gave one and a half [[volts|volt]]. \"Always check the [[voltage]] before you plug something in,\" Max said. They measured a resistor, and it had one hundred [[ohms|ohm]]. Taras laughed at a unit called the [[henry]], because it sounded like a person's name. \"It's an [[SI]] unit, just like the meter,\" Max explained. Then they built a lemon battery and pushed an [[electrode]] into each lemon. Max said that each [[ion]] carries a tiny charge through the juice. One electrode was a [[nickel]] coin, and the other was a [[zinc]] nail. Taras read that real phone batteries use [[cobalt]], not lemons. Finally, they read about a nuclear [[reactor]], but Taras still loved their tiny lemon light."},{"id":"c174","part":"p18","title":"In the chemistry lab","level":"B1","words":["hydrogen","sulfur","neon","oxide","oxygen","monoxide","dioxide","chloride","sulfate","isotope","polymer","peroxide","ether","graphite","chrome"],"story":"Anna visited her friend Olya's chemistry lab and saw a tank of [[hydrogen]] first. A yellow powder of [[sulfur]] smelled like rotten eggs, and Anna made a face. Above the door, a sign glowed with red [[neon]] light. \"Rust is iron [[oxide]], made when iron meets [[oxygen]],\" Olya said. \"Mono- means one and di- means two, so carbon [[monoxide]] and carbon [[dioxide]] are different gases.\" \"Table salt is sodium [[chloride]], and this shampoo is free of [[sulfates|sulfate]],\" she went on. Then she explained that carbon has more than one [[isotope]]. \"Plastic is a [[polymer]], and we make new ones here,\" she said proudly. When Anna cut her finger on a box, Olya cleaned it with [[peroxide]]. \"Long ago, doctors used [[ether]] to put patients to sleep,\" she added. Anna's pencil broke, and Olya joked that its [[graphite]] needed a rest. The best part was a shiny [[chrome]] machine, and Anna asked to come back soon."},{"id":"c175","part":"p18","title":"Chemistry at Home","level":"B1","words":["silicone","latex","nitrate","phosphate","ethanol","ethylene glycol","beta-carotene","pigment","mineral","cyanide"],"story":"On a rainy Sunday, Anna decided to read the labels on things at home. Mom's baking molds were made of [[silicone]], and the cleaning gloves were [[latex]]. The plant fertilizer had [[nitrate]] and [[phosphate]] for strong roots. Her hand gel was mostly [[ethanol]]. In the garage, Dad showed her the antifreeze with [[ethylene glycol]]. \"Never use an aerosol spray near a fire,\" he warned. In the kitchen, Anna read that carrots are rich in [[beta-carotene]]. Her old paint box said that every color comes from a [[pigment]]. The water bottle listed each [[mineral]], like calcium and magnesium. Dad pointed to the small alarm on the wall that warns about carbon monoxide. Anna laughed, \"The only poison here is the [[cyanide]] in my detective books!\""},{"id":"c176","part":"p18","title":"A night at the observatory","level":"B1","words":["telescope","object","asteroid","meteor","astronaut","cosmos","genesis","lander","crater","meteorite","zenith"],"story":"At the observatory on Friday, Max looked through a big [[telescope]] and saw a bright [[object]]. \"Is it a UFO?\" he whispered. \"No, it's a small [[asteroid]], a rock that circles the sun,\" the guide laughed. A minute later, a [[meteor]] burned across the sky, and Anna made a wish. Then a retired [[astronaut]] talked about the beauty of the [[cosmos]]. She explained what scientists think about the [[genesis]] of the universe. She showed a photo of a [[lander]] on Mars next to a deep [[crater]]. Then she passed around a small black stone. \"Most space rocks burn up, but this [[meteorite]] reached the ground,\" she said. The guide pointed straight up at the [[zenith]], the highest point of the sky. When Anna asked about the zodiac, the guide smiled. \"That's not science, but the stars are still beautiful.\""},{"id":"c177","part":"p18","title":"Anna's psychology experiment","level":"B1","words":["experiment","factor","element","indicator","focus","ego","alter ego","a priori","placebo","placebo effect","paradox","construct","continuum","skepticism"],"story":"For her psychology class, Anna ran an [[experiment]]: does music help people study? Noise was one [[factor]], and honesty was a key [[element]], so she explained every step. Test scores were her main [[indicator]] of success. Max kept losing [[focus]], and his low score hurt his [[ego]] a little. \"My [[alter ego]], Max the Genius, would get an A,\" he joked. \"We can't know that music helps [[a priori]]; we have to test it,\" Anna said. Half the group got \"smart candy,\" but it was only a sugar [[placebo]]. They still felt smarter, and Anna called it the [[placebo effect]]. \"What a [[paradox]]: the candy did nothing, but it worked!\" Max laughed. In her report, Anna wrote that being \"smart\" is partly a social [[construct]]. Feelings about the music formed a [[continuum]], from love to hate. Her professor praised her healthy [[skepticism]] and gave her an A."},{"id":"c178","part":"p18","title":"Genes and germs","level":"B1","words":["biotech","genome","gene","clone","microscope","mutant","microbe","toxin","enzyme","inhibitor","actin","pathogen","virus","Ebola","anthrax"],"story":"Anna's aunt Lida works at a [[biotech]] lab, and one day she invited Anna to visit. \"Here we study the human [[genome]], and every [[gene]] is part of it,\" she said. She showed a photo of a sheep and said it was a [[clone]]. Under the [[microscope]], Anna saw a [[mutant]] fly with tiny extra wings. Then Lida showed her a [[microbe]] that makes a dangerous [[toxin]]. \"This [[enzyme]] breaks the poison down, and this [[inhibitor]] stops the bug from growing,\" she explained. Next, Anna looked at muscle cells and learned that the protein [[actin]] helps them move. \"Any [[pathogen]], like a bacterium or a [[virus]], can make people sick,\" Lida said. \"Our team helps doctors fight dangerous diseases like [[Ebola]] and [[anthrax]].\" At home, Anna told Max, \"Maybe I'll become a scientist too!\""},{"id":"c179","part":"p18","title":"Brain, mood and hormones","level":"B1","words":["neuron","cortex","receptor","serotonin","antidepressant","mania","paranoia","amnesia","autism","testosterone","estrogen","insulin","adrenaline","reflex"],"story":"On Tuesday, Anna went with her friend Ira to an open lecture at medical school. The professor showed a picture of a [[neuron]], one of billions in the brain. \"This outer layer is the [[cortex]],\" she said. She explained how each [[receptor]] catches chemicals like [[serotonin]], which affects mood. \"An [[antidepressant]] can help when a person feels sad for a long time,\" she said. Then she talked about [[mania]], when people barely sleep, and [[paranoia]], when they trust no one. A student asked about [[amnesia]], when a person loses memories. The professor said that [[autism]] is simply a different way a brain develops and works. Hormones matter too, like [[testosterone]], [[estrogen]] and [[insulin]], which controls blood sugar. \"When you are scared, [[adrenaline]] makes your heart beat fast,\" she added. At the end, she tapped Ira's knee, and her leg jumped: a perfect [[reflex]]!"},{"id":"c180","part":"p18","title":"A week at medical school","level":"B1","words":["cadaver","scalpel","abdomen","appendix","pancreas","aorta","tract","anus","triage","anesthesia","anesthetic","catheter","tic","tremor","spasm","organ"],"story":"Anna's friend Ira told her about a busy week at medical school. On Monday, her anatomy group respectfully studied a [[cadaver]], and the teacher used a [[scalpel]]. They looked inside the [[abdomen]] and found the small [[appendix]]. Ira also saw the [[pancreas]], which makes insulin, and the huge [[aorta]]. The teacher said the digestive [[tract]] runs from the mouth to the [[anus]]. On Wednesday, Ira watched [[triage]] in the emergency room. A man with a broken leg had surgery under [[anesthesia]]. A little boy only needed a local [[anesthetic]] for his stitches. Later, a nurse showed Ira how to put in a [[catheter]]. An old patient with a nervous [[tic]] and a [[tremor]] in his hands told jokes. After the long day, Ira felt a sharp [[spasm]] in her back. Still, she called Anna happily: \"Today I signed up to be an [[organ]] donor!\""},{"id":"c181","part":"p18","title":"On the hospital ward","level":"B1","words":["tumor","leukemia","lymphoma","anemia","syndrome","asthma","diarrhea","vertigo","polio","penicillin","antibiotic","antidote","cholera","hospice"],"story":"On her first day on the hospital ward, Ira met many patients. A young man was happy because his [[tumor]] was not cancer. A brave girl was fighting [[leukemia]], and the man next to her had [[lymphoma]]. An old teacher was weak from [[anemia]], and a boy had a rare [[syndrome]]. A little girl showed Ira her [[asthma]] inhaler. A tourist had [[diarrhea]] after drinking tap water, and a painter had [[vertigo]]. At lunch, an old doctor told her stories about [[polio]] and the first [[penicillin]]. \"It was the first [[antibiotic]], and it saved millions of lives,\" he said. He also remembered how a quick [[antidote]] saved a farmer after a snake bite. Long ago, [[cholera]] spread through the dirty water of the city. In the evening, Ira helped a family find a quiet [[hospice]] for their grandfather. She went home tired but proud of her work."},{"id":"c182","part":"p19","title":"A castle in England","level":"B1","words":["lord","baron","duke","earl","squire","yeoman","gentry","aristocrat","monarch","throne","consort","regent","vassal","sovereign","tsar","kaiser"],"story":"Anna and Max visited an old castle in England and climbed its stone walls. A friendly guide said that a rich [[lord]] built the castle long ago. Later, a [[baron]] lived here, then a [[duke]], and then an [[earl]] bought it. A [[squire]] owned the village nearby, and each [[yeoman]] farmed his own land. The local [[gentry]] came to big dinners, and every [[aristocrat]] danced all night. Once, a [[monarch]] visited the castle and sat on a golden [[throne]]. His [[consort]] stood beside him and smiled at the guests. Their son was too young to rule, so his uncle became [[regent]]. A loyal [[vassal]] promised to protect the boy with his life. Years later, the boy became a wise [[sovereign]]. In the gallery, Anna saw portraits of a [[tsar]] and a [[kaiser]] who once visited too. At the end, Anna posed like a queen for Max's camera."},{"id":"c183","part":"p19","title":"Empires of the East","level":"B1","words":["sultan","harem","eunuch","pasha","caliph","caliphate","khan","nomad","steppe","yak","edict"],"story":"On Tuesday, Taras had a history lesson about great empires of the East. First, the teacher showed a picture of a [[sultan]] in his huge palace. The women of his family lived in a separate part called the [[harem]]. A loyal [[eunuch]] guarded its doors day and night. Far from the palace, a [[pasha]] ruled a busy port city for the sultan. Next, the class read about a wise [[caliph]] who loved books and science. His [[caliphate]] was bigger than many countries today. Then came a powerful [[khan]] and his army of horse riders. His people were [[nomads|nomad]] who moved their tents across the wide [[steppe]]. Taras laughed at a drawing of a hairy [[yak]] carrying their bags. Finally, a rich maharaja signed an [[edict]] that opened free schools for poor children. For homework, Taras drew a map of all four empires and got the best mark."},{"id":"c184","part":"p19","title":"Warriors of the Past","level":"B1","words":["gladiator","centurion","legion","paladin","fort","citadel","musketeer","duel","samurai","shogun","bastion","armada","maneuver"],"story":"Max loves military history, so he spent all Saturday with a thick book. First, he read about a brave [[gladiator]] who fought in a huge arena. A Roman [[centurion]] led a hundred men from his [[legion]] across the hills. In the next chapter, a [[paladin]] defended a small [[fort]] against a big army. When the fort fell, he ran up to the stone [[citadel]] on the hill. Max loved the part where a [[musketeer]] fought a [[duel]] at dawn. Then he read about a [[samurai]] with two swords who served the [[shogun]]. The last story was about a port town, the final [[bastion]] against an enemy [[armada]]. With a clever [[maneuver]], its few small ships hid behind an island and won. In the evening, Max told Anna every story, and she fell asleep on the sofa."},{"id":"c185","part":"p19","title":"The Wild West","level":"B1","words":["colonist","pioneer","frontier","trapper","cowboy","saloon","telegraph","bandit","dynamite","magnum","locomotive"],"story":"On Friday night, Taras watched an old western with his dad. The first [[colonists|colonist]] arrived by ship and built small towns by the sea. Years later, a family of [[pioneers|pioneer]] traveled west to the [[frontier]]. They got fifty acres of land near a quiet river. An old [[trapper]] lived alone in the forest and sold them furs. In town, a young [[cowboy]] with a revolver ordered a whiskey in the [[saloon]]. Suddenly, news came by [[telegraph]]: [[bandits|bandit]] planned to rob the afternoon train. They had [[dynamite]] and wanted to blow up the bridge. The sheriff took his big [[magnum]] and rode to the bridge with the cowboy. They got there just before the old [[locomotive]] arrived. The bandits ran away, and the train crossed safely. Taras's dad fell asleep before the end, so Taras told him the story at breakfast."},{"id":"c186","part":"p19","title":"Dark times","level":"B1","words":["imperialism","fascism","fascist","national socialist","swastika","holocaust","genocide","dictator","propaganda","dissident","junta"],"story":"On a rainy Sunday, Anna and Max visited a history museum in Kyiv. The first hall showed portraits of the last tsar and the German kaiser. A guide explained how [[imperialism]] made old empires hungry for more land. After the First World War, [[fascism]] grew in several countries in Europe. Old posters showed [[fascists|fascist]] marching in long, straight lines. In Germany, the [[national socialists|national socialist]] made the [[swastika]] their symbol. The quietest room told the story of the [[Holocaust|holocaust]], and many visitors cried there. The guide said that every [[genocide]] starts with hate and silence. In another hall, a [[dictator]] smiled from a poster full of [[propaganda]]. Next to it were letters from a brave [[dissident]] who spent years in prison. The last room showed how people stopped a military [[junta]] with peaceful protests. Outside, Anna held Max's hand and said, \"We must remember all of this.\""},{"id":"c187","part":"p19","title":"Grandma's Church","level":"B1","words":["pastor","archangel","messiah","Catholic","Catholicism","sacrament","crucifix","canon","cardinal","synod","padre","abbot","angel"],"story":"At Easter, Anna went to church with Grandma early in the morning. The [[pastor]] spoke about the [[archangel]] Michael and the coming of the [[messiah]]. After the service, they had tea with Grandma's friend Rosa, a [[Catholic]] from Lviv. Rosa explained that in [[Catholicism]], baptism and marriage are each a [[sacrament]]. She showed them a small [[crucifix]] from her mother. She also explained which old books are part of the Bible's [[canon]]. Her cousin once saw a [[cardinal]] in a red robe at a [[synod]] in Rome. Grandma remembered her own father, who met a kind [[padre]] in the army. The man prayed with the soldiers before every hard day. Later, Rosa invited them to a monastery where an old [[abbot]] makes honey. Anna said yes at once, because she loves honey more than anything. On the way home, she carried Grandma's heavy bag, and Grandma called her a real [[angel]]."},{"id":"c188","part":"p19","title":"An Evening of Many Faiths","level":"B1","words":["Protestant","Baptist","Mormon","quaker","cantor","imam","cleric","mullah","Islam","Ramadan","haram","jihad","Islamist"],"story":"Anna's college held an evening of many faiths in the big hall. First, a [[Protestant]] student talked about her church choir. A [[Baptist]] from a small town shared his family's Sunday traditions. A friendly [[Mormon]] spoke about helping neighbors, and an old [[Quaker|quaker]] talked about silence and peace. Then a Jewish [[cantor]] sang a beautiful old song. Next, an [[imam]] and another [[cleric]] came to the stage. The second man was a [[mullah]], and together they explained the basics of [[Islam]]. They told the students about fasting during [[Ramadan]] and sharing food with the poor. Pork and alcohol, they said, are [[haram]] for many Muslims. The imam explained that [[jihad]] means struggle, often to be a better person. He added that an [[Islamist]] has political goals, which is different from simply being Muslim. At the end, everyone ate cookies together, and Max ate the most."},{"id":"c189","part":"p19","title":"A yoga retreat","level":"B1","words":["retreat","swami","brahmin","chakra","karma","dharma","mantra","trance","Buddhist","lama","Buddhism","sutra","ritual","aura","Tao","yin","nirvana"],"story":"Anna's friend Lisa went on a yoga [[retreat]] in the mountains for a week. On the first day, a calm [[swami]] taught the group to breathe slowly. A [[brahmin]] from the village told them about the heart [[chakra]]. He also explained [[karma]] and [[dharma]], the idea of duty and right living. Every morning they repeated a [[mantra]], and one man even fell into a [[trance]]. On Wednesday, a [[Buddhist]] teacher came with an old [[lama]]. The old man talked about [[Buddhism]] and read a [[sutra]] in a soft voice. Lisa's favorite [[ritual]] was green tea at sunset with the group. A quiet woman with an [[aura]] of calm became her friend. She taught Lisa about the [[Tao]] and the calm force of [[yin]]. On the last day, Lisa asked her teacher how to reach [[nirvana]]. He smiled and said, \"Start by turning off your phone.\""},{"id":"c190","part":"p19","title":"Heaven, hell and spirits","level":"B1","words":["atheist","atheism","paradise","demon","antichrist","exorcism","exorcist","armageddon","dogma","inquisitor","voodoo","jinn","skeptic"],"story":"After a horror film, Max and Anna argued all the way home. Max is an [[atheist]], and his [[atheism]] makes horror films funny for him. Anna asked him if he believed in [[paradise]] or [[demons|demon]]. \"In the film, the [[antichrist]] was just a scary little boy,\" Max laughed. Anna said the [[exorcism]] scene was the worst part. Max said the [[exorcist]] looked like their math teacher. Then they argued about whether [[armageddon]] would ever come. Max said he does not like any [[dogma]], old or new. Anna called him a little [[inquisitor]] because he asked so many questions. At home, they read about [[voodoo]] and a [[jinn]] in a lamp. Anna's mom, a true [[skeptic]], said, \"No more scary stories tonight, please.\" Then she quietly checked under her own bed."},{"id":"c191","part":"p19","title":"Grandma's Folk Tales","level":"B1","words":["folklore","ghoul","banshee","leprechaun","yeti","phoenix","healer","talisman","amulet","druid","elixir","shaman","totem","idol","charlatan","enigma"],"story":"On a snowy evening, Grandma told Anna and Max old tales from world [[folklore]]. First came a hungry [[ghoul]] who lived in an old cemetery. Then a [[banshee]] cried in the night, and a tiny [[leprechaun]] hid his gold. Max liked the story of a [[yeti]] who helped lost climbers in the mountains. Anna loved the [[phoenix]] that rose again from its own ashes. A village [[healer]] gave a sick boy a [[talisman]] for luck and an [[amulet]] against illness. A [[druid]] in the forest made a magic [[elixir]] from herbs. Far away, a [[shaman]] danced around a tall [[totem]] to call the rain. The people of one tribe prayed to a golden [[idol]] in a cave. A [[charlatan]] tried to sell the villagers fake magic, but nobody bought it. \"And where did your old ring come from?\" Max asked Grandma. Grandma just smiled, and the ring stayed an [[enigma]]."},{"id":"c192","part":"p20","title":"Hey, mhm, pardon?","level":"A1","words":["hey","yo","mhm","hmm","pardon","okey-dokey","bye"],"story":"Anna: [[Hey|hey]], Max!\nMax: [[Yo|yo]], Anna! What's up?\nAnna: Let's go to the cinema tonight.\nMax: [[Mhm|mhm]]. Which film?\nAnna: [[Hmm|hmm]], maybe the funny one.\nMax: [[Pardon|pardon]]? The line is bad.\nAnna: The funny film! At six.\nMax: [[Okey-dokey|okey-dokey]]. See you at six.\nAnna: [[Bye|bye]]!"},{"id":"c193","part":"p20","title":"Wow, Max's New Flat!","level":"A2","words":["wow","ah","huh","oho","ooh la la","OMG","caramba","voila","eureka"],"story":"Max: Come in, Anna! This is my new flat.\nAnna: [[Wow|wow]]! Look at the view from this window!\nMax: Thanks. And this is my new lamp.\nAnna: [[Ah|ah]], it looks like a big orange fish. [[Huh|huh]]? Does it really work?\nMax: Yes, it does! Now look at my new jacket.\nAnna: [[Oho|oho]], very nice! [[Ooh la la|ooh la la]], you look like a movie star!\nMax: Now come into the kitchen.\nAnna: [[OMG]], what a mess! [[Caramba|caramba]], are those old pizza boxes?\nMax: Sorry! But [[voila]], my fridge is full of juice.\nMax: Wait, what is under this box? [[Eureka|eureka]]! My lost keys!\nAnna: Great! Now let's clean this kitchen together."},{"id":"c194","part":"p20","title":"Oops! A Bad Morning","level":"A2","words":["oops","brr","feh","fie","boo","mmm"],"story":"Taras: [[Oops|oops]]! I dropped my phone in the hall.\nMama: Is it OK, Taras?\nTaras: Yes, it's fine. [[Brr|brr]], the bathroom is so cold this morning!\nMama: Sorry, the heater is broken. Come and eat your soup.\nTaras: [[Feh|feh]], the soup is cold too.\nGrandpa: [[Fie|fie]] on this cold house! I sound like an old king in a film.\nAnna: [[Boo|boo]]!\nTaras: Anna! Don't jump out from behind the door!\nMama: Here, everyone. I made hot pancakes.\nTaras: [[Mmm|mmm]], they're so good! Now my morning is better."},{"id":"c195","part":"p20","title":"Ha-Ha! Movie Night","level":"A2","words":["ha","ha-ha-ha","heh","ha-ha","hehe","hee-hee","ho-ho","ho-ho-ho"],"story":"Dad: Look, the dog is wearing Grandpa's hat! [[Ha|ha]]!\nDad: And now he's dancing! [[Ha-ha-ha|ha-ha-ha]]!\nAnna: [[Heh|heh]], it's a really funny movie.\nTaras: [[Ha-ha|ha-ha]]! I'm sending this part to my friends. I wrote \"[[hehe]].\"\nSofia: [[Hee-hee|hee-hee]]! The dog fell into the cake!\nGrandpa: [[Ho-ho|ho-ho]], what do we have here? A dog in a Santa hat!\nGrandpa: [[Ho-ho-ho|ho-ho-ho]]! Merry Christmas, little dog!\nMama: Everyone is laughing. This is our best movie night."},{"id":"c196","part":"p20","title":"Stop! Bravo!","level":"A2","words":["stop","psst","achtung","basta","mayday","SOS","bravo","bravissimo","ole","vivat","banzai"],"story":"Max: [[Stop|stop]]! Nobody can go into the castle!\nAnna: [[Psst|psst]], Max, you're on the wrong side of the stage.\nTeacher: [[Achtung|achtung]], everyone! Just a joke. Now the ship scene, please.\nTeacher: [[Basta|basta]]! No more phones on stage.\nTaras: [[Mayday|mayday]]! Our plane is falling into the sea!\nAnna: We see the plane! Send an [[SOS]] to the coast!\nDad: [[Bravo|bravo]]! What a great show!\nGrandma: [[Bravissimo|bravissimo]]! I loved every minute.\nSofia: [[Olé|ole]]! Max, you were the best guard!\nGrandpa: [[Vivat|vivat]], young actors!\nMax: Thank you! Next time I want to shout \"[[banzai]]\" like soldiers in old films."},{"id":"c197","part":"p20","title":"Meow, Moo, Bam!","level":"A2","words":["meow","moo","bam","beep-beep","tick-tack","la-la","la-la-la","tra-la-la"],"story":"Anna: Grandma's village is so quiet. I can finally read my book.\nMax: Listen, the kitten says \"[[meow]].\" It wants food.\nAnna: And the cow outside says \"[[moo]].\"\nGrandpa: [[Bam|bam]]! Sorry, the wind closed the door.\nMax: Now a car is going \"[[beep-beep]]\" outside the gate.\nAnna: And the old clock in the hall goes \"[[tick-tack]].\"\nGrandma: [[La-la|la-la]]... I forgot the words of my song.\nGrandma: [[La-la-la|la-la-la]]... [[Tra-la-la|tra-la-la]]! Dinner is ready!\nAnna: This village isn't quiet, Grandma, but I love it."},{"id":"c198","part":"p20","title":"GG! Game Night","level":"A2","words":["LOL","kek","bazinga","game over","GG","blah blah blah"],"story":"Taras: Look at my hero's funny new hat!\nDmytro: [[LOL]], it looks like a banana!\nOleh: [[Kek|kek]], that's the best hat in the game.\nDmytro: Why did the robot cross the road? To charge his phone. [[Bazinga|bazinga]]!\nTaras: Oh no, the screen says \"[[Game over|game over]].\"\nOleh: Good match, everyone. [[GG]]!\nMama: Taras, dinner! All this game talk is just [[blah blah blah]] to me.\nTaras: OK, Mama, I'm coming!"},{"id":"c199","part":"p20","title":"Ciao! Hello Around the World","level":"A2","words":["ciao","arrivederci","adios","adieu","aloha","konnichiwa","sayonara","namaste","namaskar"],"story":"Max: What's in your notebook, Anna?\nAnna: Hello and goodbye words from my trips and friends.\nAnna: In Italy, people say \"[[ciao]]\" and \"[[arrivederci]].\"\nMax: And in Mexico?\nAnna: \"[[Adios|adios]].\" My friend from Paris says \"[[adieu]].\"\nMax: What about Hawaii?\nAnna: There they say \"[[aloha]].\" In Japan, I learned \"[[konnichiwa]]\" and \"[[sayonara]].\"\nMax: And India?\nAnna: My yoga teacher says \"[[namaste]].\" Her mother says \"[[namaskar]].\"\nMax: Cool! Please teach me all of them tomorrow."},{"id":"c200","part":"p20","title":"Words of Faith and Peace","level":"B1","words":["shalom","salaam","inshallah","alhamdulillah","alleluia","ave"],"story":"Anna: This evening of many faiths is lovely, and everyone greets me so warmly.\nMr. Levin: [[Shalom|shalom]], Anna! Welcome to our evening.\nAnna: Thank you! Look, there's Amira, my friend from university.\nAmira: [[Salaam|salaam]], Anna! I'm so happy you came.\nAnna: Will you come to my birthday party next Saturday?\nAmira: [[Inshallah|inshallah]], I'll be there with a cake.\nAnna: How is your mother? I heard she was sick.\nAmira: [[Alhamdulillah|alhamdulillah]], she's much better now.\nMax: Listen, the church choir is starting. They're singing \"[[Alleluia|alleluia]].\"\nAnna: And now the \"[[Ave|ave]] Maria.\" It's so beautiful and calm.\nAmira: We use different words, but tonight we all wish each other peace."}]};
